// Exámenes finales originales estilo Cambridge (Reading, Listening, Use of English, Writing, Speaking).
window.EXAMS={"1":{"reading":{"title":"A message to the class","text":"Hello, everyone! My name is Valeria Ríos, but please call me Vale. I'm a new student in this English class. Our teacher is Mr. Brown. He is very nice and he always speaks slowly. Today I'm happy and a little excited, but I'm also very tired. I don't understand every word in English, so I have a lot of questions. My classmate Daniel helps me with the answers. Thank you, Daniel! Nice to meet you all. See you tomorrow, and take care!","questions":[{"q":"What does Valeria want people to call her?","options":["Ríos","Vale","Valeria"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Ella dice please call me Vale, o sea que prefiere que le digan Vale, su nombre corto."},{"q":"Who is Mr. Brown?","options":["Her teacher","Her boss","Her classmate"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"El texto dice Our teacher is Mr. Brown. Daniel es el compañero de clase, no Mr. Brown."},{"q":"How does Valeria feel today?","options":["Happy but tired","Sad and bored","Sick and hungry"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Dice I'm happy and a little excited, but I'm also very tired: está contenta pero cansada."},{"q":"Why does Valeria have a lot of questions?","options":["She is a new coworker.","She is the teacher.","She doesn't understand every word."],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Tiene muchas preguntas porque no entiende todas las palabras en inglés: I don't understand every word."},{"q":"Who is Daniel?","options":["A student in her class","Her English teacher","Her boss at work"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Daniel es my classmate, es decir, un compañero de su clase que la ayuda."}]},"listening":{"title":"A new coworker","script":[{"who":"A","en":"Good morning! Excuse me, are you the new coworker?"},{"who":"B","en":"Yes, I am. Hi! I'm Roberto Salinas."},{"who":"A","en":"Nice to meet you, Roberto. I'm Karen. How do you spell your last name?"},{"who":"B","en":"S-A-L-I-N-A-S. And please, call me Rob."},{"who":"A","en":"Sure, Rob. How are you today?"},{"who":"B","en":"Not bad, thanks. I'm a little tired, but I'm very excited."},{"who":"A","en":"Great! Our boss is Mr. Green. He's very kind."},{"who":"B","en":"Good to know. Thank you, Karen."},{"who":"A","en":"No problem. Welcome, and have a nice day!"}],"questions":[{"q":"Where are Karen and Rob?","options":["At school","At work","At a party"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Karen pregunta si él es the new coworker, el compañero nuevo de trabajo, así que están en el trabajo."},{"q":"What is Rob's last name?","options":["Roberto","Salinas","Green"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Su apellido es Salinas y lo deletrea S-A-L-I-N-A-S. Roberto es su nombre y Green es el jefe."},{"q":"How does Rob feel?","options":["Very bored","Tired but excited","Sad and sick"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Él dice I'm a little tired, but I'm very excited: un poco cansado pero muy emocionado."},{"q":"Who is Mr. Green?","options":["Karen's classmate","A new student","Their boss"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Karen dice Our boss is Mr. Green: es el jefe de los dos."},{"q":"What time of day is it?","options":["Morning","Afternoon","Night"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Karen saluda con good morning, así que es en la mañana."}]},"use":[{"q":"___ name is Ana.","options":["I'm","Me","I","My"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Para decir mi nombre se usa el posesivo my: My name is Ana."},{"q":"A: How are you? B: I'm ___, thanks.","options":["name","sorry","fine","welcome"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"La respuesta normal a How are you? es I'm fine, thanks: estoy bien, gracias."},{"q":"___ me, can you repeat that, please?","options":["Sorry","Excuse","Thank","Please"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Para interrumpir o pedir algo con cortesía se dice Excuse me. La frase Sorry me no existe."},{"q":"I'm ___ student at this school.","options":["is","a","am","an"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Antes de una profesión o actividad se pone a: I'm a student. An se usa antes de sonido de vocal."},{"q":"A: Thank you so much! B: You're ___.","options":["fine","sorry","okay","welcome"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"La respuesta a thank you es You're welcome: de nada."},{"q":"It's lunch time and I ___ very hungry.","options":["have","am","are","is"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Tener hambre se dice con to be: I am hungry. Nunca I have hungry."},{"q":"You arrive at a party at 8 p.m. You say: Good ___, everyone!","options":["night","morning","evening","afternoon"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Al llegar en la noche se saluda con good evening. Good night es solo para despedirse o antes de dormir."},{"q":"Sorry, I don't ___ the question. Can you say it again, please?","options":["know","understand","spell","mean"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"I don't understand significa no entiendo. Por eso pides que repitan la pregunta."},{"q":"What does the word tired ___?","options":["mean","means","spell","say"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"La pregunta correcta es What does ... mean? Después de does el verbo va sin -s."},{"q":"Hi, ___! Nice to see you all today.","options":["boss","me","friend","everyone"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Para saludar a un grupo completo se usa everyone: Hi, everyone!"}],"writing":{"prompt_es":"Escribe un mensaje corto a una compañera nueva de tu clase de inglés, Sofía. Salúdala, di tu nombre completo y cómo quieres que te diga, di cómo te sientes hoy y despídete.","prompt_en":"You have a new classmate called Sofía. Write a short message to her. Say hello, tell her your full name and what she can call you, say how you feel today and say goodbye.","min_words":20,"max_words":35,"model_answer":"Hi, Sofía! My name is Carlos Mijangos, but please call me Charlie. I'm a student in your English class. Today I'm happy but a little tired. Nice to meet you! See you tomorrow.","checklist_es":["Un saludo (Hi o Hello)","Tu nombre completo y cómo te pueden llamar (call me...)","Cómo te sientes hoy con I'm + adjetivo","Una despedida (See you tomorrow, Bye, Take care)"]},"speaking":{"read_aloud":["Good morning, everyone. My name is Laura and I'm a new student.","Excuse me, can you spell that slowly, please?"],"questions":["What's your name? How do you spell your last name?","How are you today?","How do you say hello to your boss? And to a good friend?"]}},"2":{"reading":{"title":"Your new conversation partner","text":"Hi! I'm Tom Baker, your new conversation partner. I'm twenty-eight years old and I'm from Toronto, so I'm Canadian. I'm a teacher and I'm single. My birthday is in August. This is my friend Marta. She isn't Canadian. She's from Bogotá, so she's Colombian. She's thirty-one and she's married. We are in Guadalajara for work this year. My cell phone number is 333 418 2706 and my email is tombaker at fluentmail dot com. Write to me!","questions":[{"q":"Who is older?","options":["Tom","Marta","They are the same age."],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Tom tiene 28 años y Marta 31, así que Marta es mayor."},{"q":"What nationality is Tom?","options":["American","Canadian","Colombian"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Tom es de Toronto, en Canadá, por eso dice I'm Canadian."},{"q":"Which sentence about Marta is true?","options":["She is Canadian.","She is married.","She is single."],"answer":1,"explain_es":"El texto dice she's married. El soltero es Tom, y Marta no es canadiense, es colombiana."},{"q":"When is Tom's birthday?","options":["In August","In December","In April"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Tom dice My birthday is in August: su cumpleaños es en agosto."},{"q":"How can you contact Tom?","options":["Only at his school","By phone or by email","Only at his address"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Tom da su número de celular y su correo, así que puedes contactarlo por teléfono o por email."}]},"listening":{"title":"At the gym reception","script":[{"who":"A","en":"Good afternoon. Can I help you?"},{"who":"B","en":"Yes, please. I want a member card for the gym."},{"who":"A","en":"Sure. What's your name, please?"},{"who":"B","en":"Andrea Cruz. That's C-R-U-Z."},{"who":"A","en":"Thanks. And how old are you, Andrea?"},{"who":"B","en":"I'm nineteen. My birthday is in January."},{"who":"A","en":"Okay. What's your address?"},{"who":"B","en":"It's sixty Juárez Street, zip code four four six zero zero."},{"who":"A","en":"Sixteen Juárez Street?"},{"who":"B","en":"No, sorry, sixty. Six, zero."}],"questions":[{"q":"Where is Andrea?","options":["At a school","At a hospital","At a gym"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Andrea pide a member card for the gym, una credencial del gimnasio."},{"q":"How old is Andrea?","options":["Nine","Nineteen","Ninety"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Ella dice I'm nineteen: tiene 19 años. Fíjate en el final -teen."},{"q":"How does Andrea spell her last name?","options":["C-R-U-S","K-R-U-Z","C-R-U-Z"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Ella deletrea su apellido: C-R-U-Z, con C al principio y Z al final."},{"q":"What is Andrea's address?","options":["6 Juárez Street","60 Juárez Street","16 Juárez Street"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"La recepcionista entiende sixteen, pero Andrea corrige: sixty, six zero. Es el número 60."},{"q":"When is Andrea's birthday?","options":["In June","In January","In August"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Andrea dice My birthday is in January: en enero."}]},"use":[{"q":"My parents ___ from Monterrey.","options":["are","is","be","am"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Parents es plural (they), así que se usa are."},{"q":"She ___ married. She's single.","options":["not","is","isn't","aren't"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Si es soltera, no está casada: she isn't married. Con she se usa is o isn't."},{"q":"I'm twenty-five ___ old.","options":["years","age","ages","year"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"La edad se dice I'm 25 years old, con years en plural."},{"q":"Where ___ you from?","options":["are","am","do","is"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Con you se usa are: Where are you from?"},{"q":"My birthday is ___ April.","options":["of","at","on","in"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Con los meses se usa in: in April."},{"q":"Luiz is from Brazil. He's ___.","options":["Colombian","Brazil","Brazilian","Spanish"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Brazil es el país y Brazilian es la nacionalidad. Después de He's va la nacionalidad."},{"q":"Fifteen plus fifteen is ___.","options":["thirty","fifteen","thirteen","fifty"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"15 + 15 = 30, que se dice thirty. No lo confundas con thirteen, que es 13."},{"q":"They ___ Canadian. They're American.","options":["not","are","aren't","isn't"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Si son estadounidenses, no son canadienses: they aren't Canadian. Con they se usa are o aren't."},{"q":"A: What's your ___? B: It's analopez@mail.com.","options":["phone number","email","address","zip code"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"La respuesta tiene arroba, así que es un correo electrónico: email."},{"q":"I ___ twenty years old.","options":["am","have","has","is"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"En inglés la edad va con to be: I am twenty. Nunca I have twenty years."}],"writing":{"prompt_es":"Vas a tener un compañero de conversación de otro país. Escríbele un mensaje con tu nombre, tu edad, de dónde eres, el mes de tu cumpleaños y tu email.","prompt_en":"You have a new conversation partner from another country. Write a message to your partner. Tell him or her your name, your age, where you are from, the month of your birthday and your email address.","min_words":20,"max_words":35,"model_answer":"Hi! I'm Diego Ramírez. I'm twenty-two years old and I'm from Oaxaca, Mexico. My birthday is in December. I'm a student and I'm single. My email is diego22 at mail dot com.","checklist_es":["Tu nombre (I'm... o My name is...)","Tu edad con I'm ... years old","De dónde eres con I'm from...","El mes de tu cumpleaños con in","Tu correo electrónico"]},"speaking":{"read_aloud":["My phone number is five five, three nine zero, one four seven two.","She's fifteen, not fifty. Her birthday is in August."],"questions":["Where are you from?","How old are you, and when is your birthday?","What's your phone number? Say it slowly, please."]}},"3":{"reading":{"title":"My family photo","text":"Hi, I'm Sara, and this is a photo of my family. My dad is the tall man with a beard. He's very funny. My mom has long curly hair and brown eyes. She's a teacher and she's very kind. My brother Pablo is twenty. He's smart, but a little lazy! My sister Inés and I are twins. We look the same, but we are very different. She's friendly and I'm shy. My grandparents live with us. My grandmother is short and thin, and my grandfather has a big mustache.","questions":[{"q":"Who has a beard?","options":["Sara's dad","Sara's brother","Sara's grandfather"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Sara dice My dad is the tall man with a beard. El abuelo tiene bigote (mustache), no barba."},{"q":"Which word describes Sara's mom?","options":["Shy","Lazy","Kind"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Sara dice que su mamá is very kind. Lazy describe a Pablo y shy describe a Sara."},{"q":"Who is the same age as Sara?","options":["Pablo","Her grandmother","Inés"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Sara e Inés son twins, gemelas, así que tienen la misma edad."},{"q":"How are Sara and Inés different?","options":["Inés is friendly and Sara is shy.","Inés has curly hair and Sara has glasses.","Inés is tall and Sara is short."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Se ven iguales, pero su personalidad es distinta: Inés es amigable y Sara es tímida."},{"q":"Who lives in Sara's house?","options":["Sara and her aunt","Only her parents and her brother","Her parents, her brother and sister, and her grandparents"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Además de sus papás y hermanos, dice My grandparents live with us: los abuelos viven con ellos."}]},"listening":{"title":"Who's in the photo?","script":[{"who":"A","en":"Who's this woman in the photo?"},{"who":"B","en":"That's my aunt Rosa. She's my mom's sister."},{"who":"A","en":"She's pretty! Is the boy her son?"},{"who":"B","en":"Yes, that's Leo, my cousin. He's ten."},{"who":"A","en":"And the man with glasses? Is he your uncle?"},{"who":"B","en":"No, my uncle is the tall man with the beard. The man with glasses is my grandfather."},{"who":"A","en":"Really? He looks young!"},{"who":"B","en":"I know. He's seventy-two, but he's very strong and funny."},{"who":"A","en":"And who are the two girls?"},{"who":"B","en":"They're my uncle's daughters, Mia and Ana. They're twins, but Mia has short hair and Ana has long hair."}],"questions":[{"q":"Who is Rosa?","options":["B's cousin","B's mother","The sister of B's mom"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"B dice She's my mom's sister: Rosa es la hermana de su mamá, o sea su tía."},{"q":"How old is Leo?","options":["Seventy-two","Ten","Twelve"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"B dice He's ten. Setenta y dos es la edad del abuelo."},{"q":"Who is the man with glasses?","options":["B's uncle","B's father","B's grandfather"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"B corrige: el tío es el de barba y the man with glasses is my grandfather."},{"q":"What does B's uncle look like?","options":["He's tall and he has a beard.","He has glasses.","He's short and thin."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"B dice my uncle is the tall man with the beard: alto y con barba."},{"q":"What is true about Mia and Ana?","options":["They are twins with different hair.","They are B's sisters.","They both have long hair."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Son gemelas e hijas del tío (primas de B), pero Mia tiene el pelo corto y Ana largo."}]},"use":[{"q":"Carla is my mom's sister. She's my ___.","options":["uncle","aunt","cousin","niece"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"La hermana de tu mamá es tu tía: aunt. Uncle es tío."},{"q":"This is Tom and ___ wife, Ellen.","options":["their","her","our","his"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"La esposa es de Tom, un hombre, así que se usa his."},{"q":"My sister ___ long hair.","options":["has","have","are","is"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Con she (my sister) se usa has: she has long hair."},{"q":"Those are my cousins. ___ house is very big.","options":["Their","Her","They","His"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"La casa es de ellos (my cousins), así que se usa their. They es un pronombre, no posesivo."},{"q":"We have a ___.","options":["big families","family big","big family","families big"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"El adjetivo va antes del sustantivo y no cambia: a big family. Con a se usa singular."},{"q":"My father's father is my ___.","options":["grandmother","nephew","uncle","grandfather"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"El papá de tu papá es tu abuelo: grandfather."},{"q":"They have two ___, a boy and a girl.","options":["childrens","children","childs","child"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"El plural de child es irregular: children. Childs y childrens no existen."},{"q":"This is my ___ car. He loves it.","options":["brother is","brothers","brother's","brother"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Para decir de quién es algo se usa 's: my brother's car, el coche de mi hermano."},{"q":"He doesn't talk a lot with new people. He's very ___.","options":["strong","friendly","funny","shy"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Una persona que casi no habla con gente nueva es tímida: shy."},{"q":"My sister and I are twins. We look the ___.","options":["same","like","different","both"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Look the same significa vernos iguales, algo normal en gemelos."}],"writing":{"prompt_es":"Escribe sobre una persona de tu familia. Di quién es, cuántos años tiene, cómo es físicamente y cómo es su personalidad.","prompt_en":"Write about a person in your family. Say who the person is, how old he or she is, what he or she looks like, and what he or she is like.","min_words":20,"max_words":35,"model_answer":"My brother's name is Luis. He's twenty-five years old. He's tall and thin, and he has short curly hair and brown eyes. He's very funny and kind. I love him!","checklist_es":["Quién es la persona (my brother, my aunt...)","Su edad","Cómo es físicamente con is o has (tall, long hair, glasses)","Su personalidad con un adjetivo (funny, kind, shy)","Usar bien his o her"]},"speaking":{"read_aloud":["My grandmother has short curly hair and glasses.","Their children are very friendly, but their son is a little shy."],"questions":["Tell me about your family. How many people are in your family?","Describe your best friend. What does he or she look like?","Who do you look like in your family?"]}},"4":{"reading":{"title":"Apartment for rent","text":"FOR RENT: Nice two-bedroom apartment on the third floor of a quiet building in the Roma neighborhood. There is an elevator, so no stairs! The living room is big and sunny, with a new couch and a TV. The kitchen has a fridge, a stove and a microwave. There are two bathrooms, and one has a bathtub. The apartment is furnished. There isn't a garage, but there is parking on the street. Rent is 9,000 pesos a month. No pets, sorry. Call Mrs. Ortega.","questions":[{"q":"Why is the elevator good?","options":["The apartment is on the first floor.","You don't need to use the stairs.","The building is noisy."],"answer":1,"explain_es":"El anuncio dice There is an elevator, so no stairs: con el elevador no tienes que subir escaleras al tercer piso."},{"q":"What is in the living room?","options":["A fridge and a stove","A couch and a TV","A bed and a desk"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"La sala tiene a new couch and a TV. El refri y la estufa están en la cocina."},{"q":"Which sentence about the apartment is true?","options":["It doesn't have a stove.","It has only one bathroom.","It has furniture."],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Furnished significa amueblado, o sea que tiene muebles. Tiene dos baños y sí tiene estufa."},{"q":"Where can you park your car?","options":["In the yard","On the street","In the garage"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Dice There isn't a garage, but there is parking on the street: puedes estacionarte en la calle."},{"q":"Who can't rent this apartment?","options":["A student","A person with a dog","A family with two children"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"El anuncio dice No pets: no se permiten mascotas, así que una persona con perro no puede rentarlo."}]},"listening":{"title":"Where are my keys?","script":[{"who":"A","en":"Mom, where are my keys?"},{"who":"B","en":"Are they on the table in the kitchen?"},{"who":"A","en":"No, they aren't. There's a cup and a plate, but no keys."},{"who":"B","en":"Look in your bedroom. Maybe they're on your desk, next to the lamp."},{"who":"A","en":"No, they aren't there. And my bedroom is so messy!"},{"who":"B","en":"Okay. Look in the living room, under the couch."},{"who":"A","en":"Under the couch? Wait... yes! Here they are, between a pillow and a book."},{"who":"B","en":"Good. Now please clean your bedroom before dinner."}],"questions":[{"q":"What is A looking for?","options":["A phone","A book","Keys"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Desde el principio A pregunta where are my keys?: busca sus llaves."},{"q":"What is on the kitchen table?","options":["The keys","A lamp","A cup and a plate"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"A dice There's a cup and a plate, but no keys: en la mesa solo hay una taza y un plato."},{"q":"What is A's bedroom like?","options":["Messy","Clean","Quiet"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"A dice my bedroom is so messy: su cuarto está muy desordenado."},{"q":"Where are the keys?","options":["On the desk","Under the couch","In the kitchen"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Las llaves aparecen debajo del sillón de la sala, entre una almohada y un libro."},{"q":"What does Mom want A to do?","options":["Wash the dishes","Close the door","Clean the bedroom"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"La mamá dice please clean your bedroom before dinner: que limpie su cuarto."}]},"use":[{"q":"___ a big yard behind the house.","options":["There are","Is there","There is","It are"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Yard es singular (a big yard) y la oración es afirmativa: There is."},{"q":"___ two bathrooms in the apartment.","options":["There are","It's","There is","Is there"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Con dos o más cosas se usa there are."},{"q":"How many bedrooms ___ there?","options":["have","is","has","are"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"La pregunta es How many + plural + are there?"},{"q":"I can't see the cat because it's ___ the bed.","options":["next to","on","under","in front of"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Si no ves al gato es porque está debajo de la cama: under."},{"q":"The kitchen is ___ the living room and the bathroom.","options":["behind of","between","in front","next"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Between significa entre dos cosas. Next y in front necesitan to y of."},{"q":"You wash the dishes in the ___.","options":["sink","shower","closet","fridge"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Los trastes se lavan en el fregadero: sink. Shower es la regadera."},{"q":"My room is ___. There are clothes on the floor.","options":["clean","messy","sunny","quiet"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Si hay ropa en el piso, el cuarto está desordenado: messy."},{"q":"The milk is cold. It's in the ___.","options":["stove","bathtub","oven","fridge"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"La leche fría está en el refri: fridge. La estufa y el horno están calientes."},{"q":"My bedroom is on the second floor. It's ___.","options":["outside","under","downstairs","upstairs"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Si tu cuarto está en el segundo piso, está arriba: upstairs, sin in ni on."},{"q":"The apartment is ___. It has a bed, a table and a couch.","options":["furnished","dirty","noisy","cheap"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Furnished significa amueblado: ya tiene muebles como cama, mesa y sillón."}],"writing":{"prompt_es":"Tu amigo quiere saber cómo es tu casa o departamento. Escríbele un mensaje: di qué cuartos hay, cuál es tu cuarto favorito y qué cosas hay en él.","prompt_en":"Your friend wants to know about your home. Write a message to your friend. Say what rooms there are, which room is your favorite, and what is in that room.","min_words":20,"max_words":35,"model_answer":"I live in a small apartment. There are two bedrooms, a kitchen and a living room. My favorite room is my bedroom. There is a big bed and a desk next to the window.","checklist_es":["Si es casa o departamento y cómo es (small, new, quiet)","Los cuartos con there is o there are","Tu cuarto favorito","Al menos dos cosas que hay en ese cuarto y dónde están (next to, on, in)"]},"speaking":{"read_aloud":["There are three bedrooms upstairs and a big kitchen downstairs.","The lamp is on the desk, next to the window."],"questions":["Describe your bedroom. What is in it?","What is your favorite room in your home? Why?","Is your neighborhood quiet or noisy?"]}},"5":{"reading":{"title":"Welcome to Café Lupita","text":"Welcome to Café Lupita! Our breakfast is famous: eggs with beans, fresh bread and orange juice. For lunch, try our chicken soup. It's delicious, but a little spicy. Are you vegetarian? Ask for the soup without chicken, or try our cheese and avocado sandwich. Our cakes and cookies are very sweet. Coffee refills are free. You can eat here or order to go. Please tell the waiter if you are allergic to any food. Sorry, we don't take reservations on Sundays.","questions":[{"q":"What is in the famous breakfast?","options":["Cake and coffee","Eggs, beans, bread and juice","Chicken soup and bread"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"El desayuno famoso tiene huevos con frijoles, pan fresco y jugo de naranja."},{"q":"What can a vegetarian person eat?","options":["Eggs with beef","The cheese and avocado sandwich","The chicken soup"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Un vegetariano no come carne. El café le recomienda el sándwich de queso y aguacate o la sopa sin pollo."},{"q":"What is free?","options":["The orange juice","A second cup of coffee","The cookies"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Coffee refills are free: si pides otra taza de café (refill), no la pagas."},{"q":"When do you need to talk to the waiter?","options":["When you are allergic to some food","When you want a refill of soda","When you want the menu in Spanish"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"El texto pide decirle al mesero si eres alérgico a alguna comida."},{"q":"What can't you do on Sundays?","options":["Order food to go","Make a reservation","Have breakfast"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Dice we don't take reservations on Sundays: los domingos no aceptan reservaciones."}]},"listening":{"title":"At the restaurant","script":[{"who":"A","en":"Good evening. Are you ready to order?"},{"who":"B","en":"Yes. I'd like the chicken tacos, please. Are they spicy?"},{"who":"A","en":"Not very. And the hot sauce is on the table."},{"who":"B","en":"Perfect. Can I have a salad without onion? I'm allergic to onion."},{"who":"A","en":"No problem. Would you like something to drink?"},{"who":"B","en":"An orange juice, please. Oh, no, sorry. A lemonade."},{"who":"A","en":"Sure. And would you like dessert? The ice cream is delicious."},{"who":"B","en":"No, thanks. But I'd like a coffee after dinner."},{"who":"A","en":"Of course. With milk and sugar?"},{"who":"B","en":"Just milk, please. No sugar."}],"questions":[{"q":"What does B order to eat?","options":["Beef tacos and soup","Chicken tacos and a salad","Chicken soup and bread"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"B pide the chicken tacos y también a salad without onion."},{"q":"Why doesn't B want onion?","options":["B is vegetarian.","The onion is spicy.","B is allergic to it."],"answer":2,"explain_es":"B dice I'm allergic to onion: es alérgico a la cebolla."},{"q":"What does B drink with dinner?","options":["Lemonade","Water","Orange juice"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Primero pide jugo de naranja, pero cambia de idea: Oh, no, sorry. A lemonade."},{"q":"What dessert does B order?","options":["Ice cream","Nothing","Cake"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"El mesero ofrece helado, pero B dice No, thanks. Solo pide un café."},{"q":"How does B want the coffee?","options":["With sugar and no milk","With milk and no sugar","With milk and sugar"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"B dice Just milk, please. No sugar: solo con leche."}]},"use":[{"q":"Is there ___ milk in the fridge?","options":["some","many","a","any"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"En preguntas con is there se usa any: Is there any milk?"},{"q":"I'm thirsty. I'd like ___ water, please.","options":["some","any","an","many"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Al pedir algo en afirmativo se usa some: I'd like some water."},{"q":"A: ___ like some coffee? B: Yes, please.","options":["Would you","Are you","Do you","You would"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Para ofrecer algo con amabilidad se dice Would you like...? Do you like pregunta si algo te gusta en general."},{"q":"___ have the check, please?","options":["Do I","I can","Can I","Am I"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Para pedir algo se dice Can I have...? El orden es Can + I en la pregunta."},{"q":"Lemons are very ___.","options":["sour","spicy","sweet","salty"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"El limón es ácido: sour."},{"q":"I'm ___. I don't eat meat or fish.","options":["thirsty","allergic","hungry","vegetarian"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Una persona que no come carne ni pescado es vegetarian."},{"q":"You eat soup with a ___.","options":["fork","napkin","knife","spoon"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"La sopa se come con cuchara: spoon."},{"q":"Every morning I have eggs and bread for ___.","options":["breakfast","dinner","dessert","lunch"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"La comida de la mañana es el desayuno: breakfast."},{"q":"A: For here or ___ go? B: For here, please.","options":["for","to","in","at"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Para llevar se dice to go: For here or to go?"},{"q":"This soup ___ very good!","options":["taste","tastes well","is taste","tastes"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Con taste se usa un adjetivo: It tastes good. Con it o this soup el verbo lleva -s."}],"writing":{"prompt_es":"Escribe un mensaje a un amigo sobre tu restaurante favorito. Di cómo se llama, qué comida te gusta ahí, qué te gusta tomar y por qué te gusta el lugar.","prompt_en":"Write a message to a friend about your favorite restaurant. Say its name, what food you like there, what you like to drink and why you like it.","min_words":20,"max_words":35,"model_answer":"My favorite restaurant is El Fogón. The tacos are delicious and a little spicy. I like the horchata too. The food is cheap and the waiters are very friendly. Let's go there!","checklist_es":["El nombre del restaurante","Una comida y cómo sabe (delicious, spicy, sweet)","Una bebida","Una razón por la que te gusta (cheap, friendly waiters, fresh food)"]},"speaking":{"read_aloud":["I'd like the chicken soup and an orange juice, please.","Can I have the check? And a box to go, please."],"questions":["What do you have for breakfast?","What is your favorite food? Is it sweet, salty or spicy?","You are in a restaurant. Order your favorite meal and a drink."]}},"6":{"reading":{"title":"Marco's night job","text":"Marco works at night in a hospital in Monterrey. He gets up at six p.m., takes a shower and has breakfast at seven. He starts work at nine p.m. and finishes at seven a.m. Then he gets home, has dinner and goes to bed at nine in the morning. Marco works from Monday to Thursday. On Fridays, he always does the laundry and cleans the apartment. On weekends, he sleeps in, visits his parents and sometimes plays soccer. He never cooks on workdays.","questions":[{"q":"When does Marco have breakfast?","options":["At seven in the morning","At seven in the evening","At nine at night"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Marco se levanta a las seis de la tarde y desayuna a las siete, o sea, en la noche."},{"q":"How many hours does Marco work every night?","options":["Twelve","Seven","Ten"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Empieza a las 9 p.m. y termina a las 7 a.m.: son diez horas."},{"q":"What does Marco do every Friday?","options":["He does chores at home.","He works at the hospital.","He plays soccer."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Los viernes siempre lava la ropa y limpia el departamento: hace tareas de la casa (chores)."},{"q":"What does Marco do on weekends?","options":["He works at night.","He visits his parents.","He gets up at six a.m."],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Los fines de semana duerme tarde, visita a sus papás y a veces juega futbol."},{"q":"Which sentence is true?","options":["Marco sleeps during the day.","Marco cooks on Mondays.","Marco works on Saturdays."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Marco se duerme a las nueve de la mañana, así que duerme de día. Nunca cocina los días de trabajo y no trabaja los sábados."}]},"listening":{"title":"Making plans","script":[{"who":"A","en":"Hey, Luis! Do you want to go out on Saturday?"},{"who":"B","en":"Saturday? Sorry, I work on Saturdays."},{"who":"A","en":"Oh. What time do you finish?"},{"who":"B","en":"At half past two. Then I go home and take a nap."},{"who":"A","en":"Okay. How about Sunday? We can play soccer in the morning."},{"who":"B","en":"Hmm, I usually sleep in on Sundays. I get up at eleven."},{"who":"A","en":"No problem. Let's meet at a quarter past twelve, then."},{"who":"B","en":"Perfect. But I do the laundry on Sunday afternoon, so I go home at four."},{"who":"A","en":"That's fine. See you on Sunday!"}],"questions":[{"q":"Why can't Luis go out on Saturday?","options":["He is sick.","He works.","He visits his family."],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Luis dice I work on Saturdays: trabaja los sábados."},{"q":"What time does Luis finish work on Saturday?","options":["2:15","3:30","2:30"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Half past two significa dos y media: 2:30."},{"q":"What does Luis usually do on Sunday mornings?","options":["He plays soccer.","He does the laundry.","He sleeps late."],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Luis dice I usually sleep in on Sundays: duerme hasta tarde, se levanta a las once."},{"q":"What time do they meet?","options":["At 11:00","At 12:15","At 12:00"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"A quarter past twelve es doce y cuarto: 12:15."},{"q":"Why does Luis go home at four?","options":["To take a nap","To watch TV","To do a chore"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Luis lava la ropa el domingo en la tarde (do the laundry), que es una tarea de la casa."}]},"use":[{"q":"She ___ up at six every day.","options":["get","gets","is get","getting"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"En presente simple con she el verbo lleva -s: she gets up."},{"q":"I ___ breakfast on weekdays. I'm always late!","options":["never has","have never","don't never have","never have"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"El adverbio de frecuencia va antes del verbo: I never have. En inglés no se usa doble negación."},{"q":"My class starts ___ eight o'clock.","options":["at","on","to","in"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Con las horas se usa at: at eight o'clock."},{"q":"We go to the market ___ Saturdays.","options":["in","to","at","on"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Con los días de la semana se usa on: on Saturdays."},{"q":"It's 3:30. It's half ___ three.","options":["quarter","past","to","after"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Las tres y media se dice half past three."},{"q":"A: ___ does your brother finish work? B: At five.","options":["Who","Where","How many","What time"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"La respuesta es una hora (at five), así que la pregunta es What time."},{"q":"My dad ___ TV in the evening.","options":["watch","watches","watchs","watching"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Con he o she, los verbos que terminan en ch agregan -es: watches."},{"q":"I clean the house ___ a week, on Sundays.","options":["once","one","every","sometimes"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Una vez a la semana se dice once a week."},{"q":"After dinner, I ___ the dishes.","options":["take","make","sleep","wash"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Lavar los trastes se dice wash the dishes (o do the dishes). Make the dishes no existe."},{"q":"My brother doesn't ___ on Sundays. He sleeps in.","options":["working","work","works","to work"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Después de doesn't el verbo va en forma base, sin -s: he doesn't work."}],"writing":{"prompt_es":"Escribe sobre un sábado normal para ti. Di a qué hora te levantas y qué haces en la mañana, en la tarde y en la noche. Usa por lo menos una palabra de frecuencia (always, usually, sometimes, never).","prompt_en":"Write about a typical Saturday for you. Say what time you get up and what you do in the morning, in the afternoon and in the evening. Use at least one word like always, usually, sometimes or never.","min_words":20,"max_words":35,"model_answer":"On Saturdays I get up at nine. In the morning I always clean the house and do the laundry. In the afternoon I sometimes visit my grandparents. At night I go out with friends.","checklist_es":["La hora a la que te levantas con at","Qué haces en la mañana, en la tarde y en la noche","Al menos un adverbio de frecuencia antes del verbo","Verbos en presente simple (I get up, I clean...)"]},"speaking":{"read_aloud":["I usually get up at half past six and take a shower.","She never goes to bed before midnight on weekends."],"questions":["What time do you get up on weekdays?","What do you do in your free time?","Which chores do you do at home, and how often?"]}},"7":{"reading":{"title":"Which dress?","text":"Hi Jess! I'm at Moda Store and there's a big sale this week. Everything is thirty percent off! I'm looking for a dress for Ana's party on Saturday. There's a long blue dress for sixty dollars and a short red one for forty-five. The red one is cheaper, but the blue one is cotton and it's more comfortable. I prefer the blue one, but it's a size medium and I usually wear small. I think a medium is too loose for me. The cashier says exchanges are okay if it doesn't fit, but there are no refunds on sale items. What do you think? Which one is better? Call me, I'm here until seven! Love, Mariana","questions":[{"q":"Why is Mariana shopping?","options":["She needs a dress for a party.","She wants a gift for Jess.","She wants to return a dress."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Mariana dice I'm looking for a dress for Ana's party: busca un vestido para una fiesta."},{"q":"What is true about the blue dress?","options":["It costs more, but it's more comfortable.","It's short and made of cotton.","It's cheaper than the red one."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"El azul cuesta 60 dólares y el rojo 45, pero el azul es de algodón y más cómodo. Además el azul es largo."},{"q":"What is the problem with the blue dress?","options":["It isn't her usual size.","It isn't on sale.","It's too tight."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"El vestido es talla mediana y ella normalmente usa chica, por eso piensa que le queda flojo, no apretado."},{"q":"If the dress doesn't fit, what can Mariana do?","options":["Change it for a different one","Get her money back","Nothing at all"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Puede hacer un exchange (cambiarlo por otro), pero no hay refund (devolución de dinero) en artículos de oferta."},{"q":"What does Mariana want Jess to do?","options":["Come to the store","Buy the red dress","Give her opinion"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Mariana pregunta What do you think? Which one is better?: quiere la opinión de Jess."}]},"listening":{"title":"Buying sneakers","script":[{"who":"A","en":"Hi, can I help you?"},{"who":"B","en":"Yes, I'm looking for sneakers. How much are these white ones?"},{"who":"A","en":"Those are eighty-five dollars. But these gray ones are on sale. They're only fifty-five."},{"who":"B","en":"Oh, they're much cheaper. Can I try them on? I'm a size eight."},{"who":"A","en":"Sure, here you go. How do they fit?"},{"who":"B","en":"Hmm, they're a little tight. Do you have them in an eight and a half?"},{"who":"A","en":"Let me check. Yes, here you are."},{"who":"B","en":"These are perfect. I'll take them. Can I pay by credit card?"},{"who":"A","en":"Of course. Here's your receipt. You have thirty days to exchange them."}],"questions":[{"q":"Which sneakers does B try on?","options":["The white ones","The black ones","The gray ones"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"B prueba los grises porque están en oferta y son más baratos que los blancos."},{"q":"How much are the gray sneakers?","options":["Eighty-five dollars","Fifty-five dollars","Forty-five dollars"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"La vendedora dice these gray ones are on sale. They're only fifty-five."},{"q":"What is wrong with the first pair B tries on?","options":["They're too expensive.","She doesn't like the color.","They're too tight."],"answer":2,"explain_es":"B dice they're a little tight: le quedan apretados."},{"q":"What size does B buy?","options":["Nine","Eight","Eight and a half"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"La talla ocho le aprieta, así que pide y compra la ocho y media."},{"q":"What can B do in the next thirty days?","options":["Exchange the sneakers","Get a discount on boots","Pay with cash"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"La vendedora dice You have thirty days to exchange them: puede cambiarlos durante 30 días."}]},"use":[{"q":"These shoes are ___ than those boots.","options":["cheaper","more cheap","cheapest","cheap"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Cheap es un adjetivo corto, así que el comparativo es cheaper than."},{"q":"This jacket is ___ expensive than that one.","options":["more","most","very","much"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Expensive es un adjetivo largo, así que el comparativo es more expensive than."},{"q":"How much ___ these jeans?","options":["do","is","are","does"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Jeans siempre es plural, así que se dice How much are these jeans?"},{"q":"I really like ___ sunglasses over there.","options":["that","those","this","these"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Para cosas en plural que están lejos (over there) se usa those."},{"q":"These pants are too ___. I need a bigger size.","options":["long","tight","loose","cheap"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Si necesitas una talla más grande es porque el pantalón te aprieta: tight."},{"q":"A: Can I help you? B: No, thanks. I'm just ___.","options":["look","watching","looking","seeing"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Cuando no necesitas ayuda en una tienda se dice I'm just looking: solo estoy viendo."},{"q":"I want to return this sweater. Here's my ___.","options":["cash","receipt","change","discount"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Para devolver algo te piden el comprobante de compra: receipt."},{"q":"Your sweater is nice, but I think mine is ___.","options":["gooder","best","more good","better"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"El comparativo de good es irregular: better. Gooder y more good no existen."},{"q":"Which one do you ___, the striped shirt or the plain one?","options":["prefer","prefers","are prefer","preferring"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Después de do you el verbo va en forma base: Which one do you prefer?"},{"q":"I can't wear these jeans. I want to ___ them for a bigger size.","options":["pay","exchange","refund","cost"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Cambiar algo por otra cosa (otra talla) es exchange. Refund es que te regresen el dinero."}],"writing":{"prompt_es":"Escríbele un email a un amigo sobre algo que quieres comprar. Di qué es, de qué color y talla, cuánto cuesta y por qué lo prefieres en lugar de otra opción. Invita a tu amigo a ir de compras contigo.","prompt_en":"Write an email to a friend about something you want to buy. Say what it is, its color and size, how much it costs, and why you prefer it to another one. Invite your friend to go shopping with you.","min_words":25,"max_words":50,"model_answer":"Hi Rita! There's a big sale at the mall this week. I want to buy a black jacket in size medium for forty dollars. The gray one is more expensive and a little tight. The black one is more comfortable. Do you want to come with me on Saturday?","checklist_es":["Qué quieres comprar, con color y talla","El precio","Una comparación con otra opción (cheaper, more comfortable, better than)","Una invitación a tu amigo (Do you want to come...?)"]},"speaking":{"read_aloud":["Excuse me, how much are these striped sweaters?","The cotton shirt is cheaper and more comfortable than the other one."],"questions":["What clothes do you usually wear on weekends?","Do you prefer shopping online or at the mall? Why?","Think of two stores in your city. Which one is better, and why?"]}},"8":{"reading":{"title":"How to get to my place","text":"Hi Alex! Welcome to Guadalajara! Here's how to get to my apartment from the airport. Don't take a taxi at the door, because they're very expensive. Take the airport bus to the central station. It usually takes about forty minutes, but it can take more at rush hour. At the station, get off and take the subway to Plaza Patria. That's four stops. When you come out of the station, turn left and walk straight ahead for two blocks. My building is across from a big pharmacy, between a bank and a small park. I'm working right now, so my neighbor Mrs. Paz is waiting for you with the keys. She lives on the first floor. Send me a message when you arrive! Diego","questions":[{"q":"Why does Diego say not to take a taxi?","options":["It's very slow.","It costs a lot.","There aren't any at the airport."],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Diego dice they're very expensive: los taxis del aeropuerto son muy caros."},{"q":"How long is the bus trip when there isn't much traffic?","options":["About two hours","Four stops","About forty minutes"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"El camión hace unos cuarenta minutos. A la hora pico (rush hour) puede tardar más. Cuatro paradas es el metro."},{"q":"Which types of transport does Alex need?","options":["A bus and the subway","A train and the subway","A taxi and a bus"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Alex toma el camión del aeropuerto y luego el metro hasta Plaza Patria. No toma taxi."},{"q":"Where is Diego's building?","options":["Behind a small park","On the other side of the street from a pharmacy","Next to a pharmacy"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Across from significa enfrente, cruzando la calle. El edificio está entre un banco y un parque."},{"q":"Why isn't Diego at home?","options":["He is at the airport.","He is at the pharmacy.","He is at work."],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Diego dice I'm working right now: está trabajando, por eso su vecina tiene las llaves."}]},"listening":{"title":"Late for the movie","script":[{"who":"A","en":"Hi, Sam? Where are you? The movie starts in twenty minutes!"},{"who":"B","en":"I know, I'm so sorry! I'm on the bus right now, but there's a lot of traffic."},{"who":"A","en":"Oh no. Where are you exactly?"},{"who":"B","en":"We're crossing the bridge near the museum. The bus is moving really slowly."},{"who":"A","en":"Okay, get off at the next stop and take the subway. It's faster."},{"who":"B","en":"Good idea. Which station?"},{"who":"A","en":"Get on at Hidalgo and get off at Centro. The theater is around the corner from the station, next to the post office."},{"who":"B","en":"How long does it take on the subway?"},{"who":"A","en":"About ten minutes. Hurry up!"}],"questions":[{"q":"Why is Sam late?","options":["There is a lot of traffic.","Sam is lost.","Sam missed the bus."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Sam dice I'm on the bus right now, but there's a lot of traffic: va en el camión pero hay mucho tráfico."},{"q":"Where is Sam right now?","options":["Inside the museum","On a bridge, on the bus","At a subway station"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Sam dice We're crossing the bridge near the museum: el camión está cruzando un puente."},{"q":"What does A tell Sam to do?","options":["Take a taxi","Stay on the bus","Get off the bus and take the subway"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"A le dice get off at the next stop and take the subway porque el metro es más rápido."},{"q":"Where is the movie theater?","options":["Across from the museum","Inside Hidalgo station","Next to the post office"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"El cine está a la vuelta de la estación Centro, junto a la oficina de correos."},{"q":"How long is the trip on the subway?","options":["Twenty minutes","About an hour","About ten minutes"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"A dice About ten minutes. Veinte minutos es lo que falta para que empiece la película."}]},"use":[{"q":"Go straight and ___ left at the traffic light.","options":["turns","turning","turn","to turn"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Las indicaciones usan el imperativo: el verbo en forma base sin sujeto, turn left."},{"q":"Shh! Dad ___ on the phone right now.","options":["talking","talks","is talking","talk"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Para algo que pasa en este momento (right now) se usa el presente continuo: is talking."},{"q":"I usually go to school ___ bus.","options":["with","by","on","in"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Con medios de transporte se usa by sin artículo: by bus, by car."},{"q":"I live near my office, so I go to work ___ foot.","options":["in","by","at","on"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"A pie se dice on foot, no by foot."},{"q":"A: ___ is it from here to the airport? B: About twenty kilometers.","options":["How much","How far","How long","How many"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"La respuesta es una distancia en kilómetros, así que se pregunta How far."},{"q":"___ cross the street here. It's dangerous.","options":["Not","Doesn't","Don't","No"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"El imperativo negativo se forma con Don't + verbo: Don't cross."},{"q":"The pharmacy is ___ the street from the bank. Just cross and you're there.","options":["in front","between","next","across"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Across the street from significa enfrente, del otro lado de la calle."},{"q":"Our flight is ___. It's leaving two hours late.","options":["careful","delayed","fast","crowded"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Si el vuelo sale tarde, está retrasado: delayed."},{"q":"It ___ thirty minutes to get downtown by subway.","options":["does","has","makes","takes"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Para decir cuánto tiempo se hace a un lugar se usa It takes + tiempo."},{"q":"Be ___! There's a lot of traffic on this highway.","options":["caring","care","carefully","careful"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Después de be va un adjetivo: Be careful, ten cuidado."}],"writing":{"prompt_es":"Una amiga va a visitarte por primera vez. Escríbele un mensaje para explicarle cómo llegar a tu casa desde una estación de metro o de camión. Di qué transporte tomar, cuánto tiempo se hace y cómo llegar caminando. Menciona un lugar que está cerca de tu casa.","prompt_en":"A friend is visiting you for the first time. Write a message to explain how to get to your home from a subway or bus station. Say what transport to take, how long it takes and how to walk there. Mention a place near your home.","min_words":25,"max_words":50,"model_answer":"Hi Paola! Take the subway to Insurgentes station. It takes about twenty minutes. When you get off, turn right and walk straight ahead for two blocks. My building is across from a big supermarket, next to a bank. See you soon!","checklist_es":["Qué transporte tomar (take the subway, take the bus)","Cuánto tiempo se hace con It takes...","Indicaciones con imperativos (turn right, walk straight ahead, cross)","Un lugar cercano con preposición (across from, next to, between)"]},"speaking":{"read_aloud":["Go straight ahead for two blocks and turn left at the traffic light.","Our flight is delayed, so we're waiting at the gate right now."],"questions":["How do you get to work or school? How long does it take?","Give directions from your home to a supermarket near you.","What are the people in your home doing right now?"]}},"9":{"reading":{"title":"A weekend in Puerto Escondido","text":"Last month, my sister and I traveled to Puerto Escondido for a long weekend. We took a night bus from Oaxaca City. The trip was ten hours long and I didn't sleep at all! We stayed in a small hotel near the beach. On Saturday morning we swam in the ocean, and then we ate fish tacos at a little restaurant. They were delicious. After that, my sister bought souvenirs for our parents. On Sunday I lost my phone on the beach and I was very sad. But that evening, a young surfer came to our hotel with it. He found it in the sand! We invited him to dinner to say thank you. Finally, on Monday, we flew home. It was much faster!","questions":[{"q":"How did they travel to Puerto Escondido?","options":["By plane","By bus","By car"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Dice We took a night bus from Oaxaca City. En avión (flew) fue solo el regreso."},{"q":"Why was the bus trip hard for the writer?","options":["The bus was crowded.","The bus was delayed.","The writer didn't sleep."],"answer":2,"explain_es":"El viaje duró diez horas y I didn't sleep at all: no durmió nada."},{"q":"Who were the souvenirs for?","options":["The writer's parents","The surfer","The writer's sister"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"La hermana compró recuerdos for our parents, para sus papás."},{"q":"What happened on Sunday?","options":["The writer lost a phone, and a surfer returned it.","The writer bought a new phone.","The writer met their parents at the beach."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"El domingo perdió su celular en la playa y en la tarde un surfista lo llevó al hotel."},{"q":"Why did they have dinner with the surfer?","options":["Because he was an old friend","Because he worked at the hotel","To thank him for his help"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Lo invitaron a cenar to say thank you, para darle las gracias por regresar el celular."}]},"listening":{"title":"How was your weekend?","script":[{"who":"A","en":"Hi, Pete! How was your weekend?"},{"who":"B","en":"It was great, thanks. I went to my cousin's wedding in Querétaro."},{"who":"A","en":"Oh, nice! Did you drive there?"},{"who":"B","en":"No, I didn't. My car is at the mechanic's, so I took the bus on Friday night."},{"who":"A","en":"And how was the wedding?"},{"who":"B","en":"So much fun! I danced a lot and I met some really nice people. But I ate too much cake!"},{"who":"A","en":"Ha! What did you do on Sunday?"},{"who":"B","en":"I slept until noon, and then I came home. What about you?"},{"who":"A","en":"Oh, it was boring. I stayed home and studied for my English exam."}],"questions":[{"q":"Why did Pete go to Querétaro?","options":["For a wedding","For a vacation at the beach","For work"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Pete fue a la boda de su primo: my cousin's wedding."},{"q":"How did Pete travel?","options":["By plane","By bus","By car"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Pete dice I took the bus on Friday night."},{"q":"Why didn't Pete drive?","options":["His car had a problem.","He doesn't have a car.","He was very tired."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Su coche está en el taller (at the mechanic's), o sea que tenía un problema."},{"q":"What did Pete do on Sunday morning?","options":["He studied.","He slept.","He danced."],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Pete dice I slept until noon: durmió hasta el mediodía."},{"q":"How was A's weekend?","options":["Boring","Great","Fun"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"A dice it was boring: se quedó en casa estudiando para su examen."}]},"use":[{"q":"I ___ at home all day yesterday.","options":["were","was","am","be"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"El pasado de to be con I es was."},{"q":"We ___ a great movie last night.","options":["watching","watches","watched","watch"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Last night indica pasado. Watch es regular, así que se agrega -ed: watched."},{"q":"They ___ to Cancún last summer.","options":["went","goed","gone","go"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Go es irregular: su pasado es went. Goed no existe."},{"q":"___ you see the game on Sunday?","options":["Did","Were","Was","Do"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Las preguntas en pasado con verbos normales usan Did + verbo en forma base."},{"q":"I didn't ___ breakfast this morning.","options":["eating","eat","ate","eaten"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Después de didn't el verbo regresa a su forma base: I didn't eat."},{"q":"My parents ___ married in 1995.","options":["got","did get","get","were get"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Casarse en pasado es got married. Get es irregular y su pasado es got."},{"q":"I met my best friend ten years ___.","options":["ago","before","last","past"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Hace diez años se dice ten years ago, con ago al final."},{"q":"He ___ a lot for the exam last week.","options":["study","studys","studyed","studied"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Study termina en consonante + y, así que en pasado cambia a -ied: studied."},{"q":"A: ___ was your vacation? B: It was amazing!","options":["Who","How","When","What"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"La respuesta describe cómo estuvo (amazing), así que se pregunta How was...?"},{"q":"First we had dinner. ___ that, we went dancing.","options":["Then","Finally","After","Suddenly"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"La expresión es After that: después de eso. Then that y Finally that no son correctas."}],"writing":{"prompt_es":"Escríbele un email a un amigo sobre tu fin de semana pasado. Di a dónde fuiste o con quién estuviste, dos cosas que hiciste y cómo estuvo. Termina con una pregunta para tu amigo.","prompt_en":"Write an email to a friend about last weekend. Say where you went or who you were with, two things you did and how it was. End with a question for your friend.","min_words":25,"max_words":50,"model_answer":"Hi Andrés! Last weekend I went to Puebla with my family. On Saturday we visited some old churches and ate mole. On Sunday we bought souvenirs for my grandparents. It was a great trip, but I was very tired! How was your weekend?","checklist_es":["A dónde fuiste o con quién (I went to..., I was with...)","Dos actividades en pasado simple (regulares e irregulares)","Cómo estuvo con was (It was great, fun, boring)","Una pregunta final como How was your weekend?"]},"speaking":{"read_aloud":["Last summer we traveled to the beach and stayed in a small hotel.","I didn't go out on Saturday. I watched a movie and slept early."],"questions":["What did you do last weekend?","Tell me about your last vacation. Where did you go and what did you do?","What did you eat yesterday?"]}},"10":{"reading":{"title":"Job opening: part-time salesperson","text":"Sol Shoes is hiring! We are a family store in downtown Mérida and we need a friendly part-time salesperson for weekends and Wednesday afternoons. You don't have to have experience, because we give training. But you have to speak English and Spanish, because a lot of our customers are tourists. You also have to be on time and wear our uniform: a blue shirt and black pants. We give you the shirt. The salary is 1,500 pesos a week, plus a discount on all our shoes. Can you use a computer? Great, but it isn't necessary. To apply, send your resume by email before Friday, May 9. The next week, we call the best people for an interview. Last year we hired three students, and they loved it!","questions":[{"q":"When does the salesperson work?","options":["Every evening","From Monday to Friday","On weekends and Wednesday afternoons"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"El anuncio busca a alguien for weekends and Wednesday afternoons."},{"q":"Who can apply for this job?","options":["Only people with a lot of experience","Only people who speak English","A person with no experience who speaks two languages"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"No es necesario tener experiencia (you don't have to), pero sí hay que hablar inglés y español."},{"q":"What does the store give the new salesperson?","options":["Black pants","A shirt","A computer"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Dice We give you the shirt. Los pantalones negros los tiene que poner la persona."},{"q":"What is NOT necessary for this job?","options":["Speaking English","Computer skills","Being on time"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Sobre la computadora dice it isn't necessary. Hablar inglés y llegar a tiempo sí son obligatorios (have to)."},{"q":"What happens after Friday, May 9?","options":["The store hires three students.","The store invites some people to an interview.","The store has a big sale."],"answer":1,"explain_es":"La semana siguiente llaman a las mejores personas para una entrevista. Los tres estudiantes fueron el año pasado."}]},"listening":{"title":"A job interview","script":[{"who":"A","en":"Good morning, Ms. Herrera. Please sit down. So, you applied for the receptionist job."},{"who":"B","en":"Yes, I saw the ad online last week."},{"who":"A","en":"Great. Tell me about your experience."},{"who":"B","en":"I worked at a hotel in Cancún for two years. I answered the phone and helped guests with their reservations."},{"who":"A","en":"Very good. Can you speak any other languages?"},{"who":"B","en":"I can speak English and Spanish well. I can speak a little French, but not very well."},{"who":"A","en":"The job is full-time, and sometimes you have to work on Saturdays. Is that a problem?"},{"who":"B","en":"No, that's fine. Do I have to wear a uniform?"},{"who":"A","en":"No, you don't. You just have to dress formally. The salary is twelve thousand pesos a month."},{"who":"B","en":"That sounds good. Thank you for your time."}],"questions":[{"q":"What job is the interview for?","options":["Salesperson","Hotel manager","Receptionist"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"El entrevistador dice you applied for the receptionist job."},{"q":"Where did Ms. Herrera work before?","options":["At an airport","At a school","At a hotel"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Ella dice I worked at a hotel in Cancún for two years."},{"q":"Which language does Ms. Herrera speak badly?","options":["English","French","Spanish"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Ella dice que habla un poco de francés, but not very well. Inglés y español los habla bien."},{"q":"What does she sometimes have to do in the new job?","options":["Work on Saturdays","Wear a uniform","Travel to Cancún"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"El entrevistador dice sometimes you have to work on Saturdays."},{"q":"What is true about the uniform?","options":["She doesn't have to wear one.","She has to buy one.","She has to wear it on Saturdays."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Cuando ella pregunta por el uniforme, la respuesta es No, you don't: no es necesario, solo vestir formal."}]},"use":[{"q":"My sister is ___ engineer.","options":["the","a","an","one"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Antes de una profesión va a o an. Engineer empieza con sonido de vocal, así que es an engineer."},{"q":"She ___ drive, but she can't fix a car.","options":["can to","is can","cans","can"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Can no cambia con she y el verbo va después sin to: she can drive."},{"q":"Paul ___ wear a uniform at work.","options":["has","must to","has to","have to"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Para obligación con he o she se usa has to + verbo."},{"q":"Tomorrow is a holiday, so we ___ go to the office.","options":["don't have to","doesn't have to","has to","have to"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Si es día festivo no es necesario ir: we don't have to. Con we se usa don't, no doesn't."},{"q":"I ___ my homework every evening.","options":["do","have","take","make"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Con homework se usa do: I do my homework."},{"q":"My brother is a ___. He fixes cars.","options":["lawyer","firefighter","accountant","mechanic"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"La persona que arregla coches es el mecánico: mechanic."},{"q":"A: Did you ___ the exam? B: Yes! I got a good grade.","options":["fail","lose","approve","pass"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Aprobar un examen es pass. Approve es un falso amigo que significa estar de acuerdo o autorizar."},{"q":"Yesterday I ___ stay late to finish the report.","options":["has to","must","have to","had to"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Yesterday indica pasado. El pasado de have to es had to para todas las personas."},{"q":"The meeting starts at ten, so please be ___ time.","options":["on","in","by","at"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Ser puntual se dice be on time."},{"q":"I work twenty hours a week. It's a ___ job.","options":["full-time","salary","deadline","part-time"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Veinte horas a la semana es medio tiempo: a part-time job."}],"writing":{"prompt_es":"Viste un anuncio de trabajo de medio tiempo en una tienda. Escribe un email corto para solicitar el empleo. Di qué trabajo quieres, tu experiencia, dos cosas que sabes hacer (can) y cuándo puedes trabajar.","prompt_en":"You saw an ad for a part-time job in a store. Write a short email to apply for the job. Say which job you want, your experience, two things you can do, and when you can work.","min_words":25,"max_words":50,"model_answer":"Dear Ms. López, I want to apply for the part-time salesperson job. I worked at a clothing store for one year. I can speak English and Spanish, and I can use a computer well. I can work on weekends. Thank you, Ana Ruiz","checklist_es":["Un saludo formal (Dear...) y una despedida","El trabajo que quieres con apply for","Tu experiencia (I worked at... o I have experience in...)","Dos habilidades con can","Cuándo puedes trabajar"]},"speaking":{"read_aloud":["I applied for a full-time job, and I have an interview on Monday.","Nurses sometimes have to work at night, but teachers don't have to."],"questions":["What do you do? Do you work or study?","What can you do well? What can't you do?","What do you have to do every day at work or at school?"]}},"11":{"reading":{"title":"An email to a friend","text":"Hi Emma,\n\nSorry I didn't come to your party on Saturday. On Friday night I had a terrible headache and a sore throat, and on Saturday morning I had a fever too. My mom took me to the doctor. She looked at my throat and my ears and said I had an infection. She gave me a prescription for some medicine. I have to take one pill three times a day, after meals. She also said I should drink a lot of water and stay in bed for two days.\n\nI'm feeling much better now, but my back hurts because I stayed in bed all weekend! The doctor said I shouldn't go to the gym this week, so I'm going to watch movies at home. Can you tell me about the party? I want to see your photos.\n\nLove,\nSofia","questions":[{"q":"Why didn't Sofia go to Emma's party?","options":["She had to work.","She was sick.","She was at the gym.","Her mom was sick."],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Sofia dice que tenía dolor de cabeza, dolor de garganta y fiebre, o sea, estaba enferma."},{"q":"When did Sofia have a fever?","options":["On Sunday","All week","On Saturday morning","On Friday night"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"El viernes en la noche tenía dolor de cabeza y de garganta; la fiebre empezó el sábado en la mañana."},{"q":"How often does Sofia take her medicine?","options":["Only when her head hurts","Three times a day, after meals","Two times a day, with water","Once a day, before breakfast"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"El correo dice: one pill three times a day, after meals, es decir, tres veces al día después de comer."},{"q":"What did the doctor say Sofia shouldn't do this week?","options":["Drink a lot of water","Take her medicine","Go to the gym","Stay at home"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"La doctora dijo: you shouldn't go to the gym this week. Las otras opciones sí son cosas que debe hacer."},{"q":"Why does Sofia's back hurt?","options":["She carried heavy boxes.","She stayed in bed a lot.","She fell at the party.","She went to the gym."],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Sofia explica que le duele la espalda porque se quedó en cama todo el fin de semana."}]},"listening":{"title":"At the doctor's office","script":[{"who":"A","en":"Good morning. What's the problem today?"},{"who":"B","en":"Hi, doctor. I fell while I was playing soccer yesterday, and now my right wrist hurts a lot."},{"who":"A","en":"I see. Can you move your fingers?"},{"who":"B","en":"Yes, but it hurts when I move my hand up and down."},{"who":"A","en":"Did you put any ice on it?"},{"who":"B","en":"Yes, my sister gave me some ice last night, and I took two pills for the pain."},{"who":"A","en":"OK. I don't think it's broken, but we should take an X-ray to be sure."},{"who":"B","en":"Is it going to take a long time? I have to go to work at two."},{"who":"A","en":"No, about twenty minutes. And you shouldn't play soccer for three weeks."},{"who":"B","en":"Three weeks? Oh no, we have a big game next Saturday!"},{"who":"A","en":"I'm sorry, but your health is more important. Are you allergic to any medicine?"},{"who":"B","en":"No, I'm not."}],"questions":[{"q":"How did the man hurt himself?","options":["He cut his hand at work.","He fell while he was playing soccer.","He fell off his bike.","He hit his hand on a door."],"answer":1,"explain_es":"El paciente dice: I fell while I was playing soccer yesterday."},{"q":"What part of his body hurts?","options":["His head","His left foot","His back","His right wrist"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Dice claramente que le duele la muñeca derecha: my right wrist hurts a lot."},{"q":"What did he do last night?","options":["He went to the hospital.","He played another game.","He called the doctor.","He put ice on it and took some pills."],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Su hermana le dio hielo y él se tomó dos pastillas para el dolor."},{"q":"What does the doctor want to do?","options":["Call an ambulance","Take an X-ray","Send him home","Give him a prescription"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"La doctora dice: we should take an X-ray to be sure, o sea, sacar una radiografía."},{"q":"Why is the man unhappy at the end?","options":["The X-ray takes two hours.","He can't play in a big game.","He can't go to work.","He is allergic to the medicine."],"answer":1,"explain_es":"No puede jugar futbol por tres semanas y tiene un partido importante el próximo sábado."}]},"use":[{"q":"My feet ___ because I walked all day.","options":["hurted","hurting","hurts","hurt"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Feet es plural, así que el verbo va sin -s: my feet hurt. Hurt es irregular y no existe hurted."},{"q":"I ___ a terrible headache right now.","options":["am","do","feel of","have"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Para síntomas se usa have: I have a headache. Nunca I am headache."},{"q":"You ___ see a doctor about that cough.","options":["should to","must to","shoulds","should"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Después de should va el verbo base sin to y should no cambia con he, she o it."},{"q":"Can you give me some ___ about my diet?","options":["a advices","advice","advices","an advice"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Advice es incontable: some advice o a piece of advice, nunca advices ni an advice."},{"q":"Last week my brother ___ his leg playing basketball.","options":["break","broke","broken","breaked"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Break es irregular: el pasado es broke. Broken es el participio."},{"q":"The dentist checked all my ___.","options":["tooths","teeths","tooth","teeth"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Tooth tiene plural irregular: one tooth, two teeth, igual que foot y feet."},{"q":"Are you allergic ___ any food?","options":["with","at","of","to"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"En inglés se dice allergic to, con la preposición to."},{"q":"Don't forget to ___ your medicine after dinner.","options":["do","take","put","make"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Con medicinas y pastillas se usa take: take your medicine, take a pill."},{"q":"I ___ off my bike yesterday and cut my knee.","options":["felt","fall","fell","falled"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Fall es irregular: fall, fell, fallen. Felt es el pasado de feel (sentir)."},{"q":"The doctor gave me a ___ for some antibiotics.","options":["ticket","recipe","receipt","prescription"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"La receta del doctor es prescription. Recipe es una receta de cocina y receipt es un comprobante de compra."}],"writing":{"prompt_es":"Escribe un correo a tu maestra de inglés, la Sra. López. Dile que no puedes ir a clase mañana, explica qué síntomas tienes, cuenta qué te dijo el doctor y pregúntale por la tarea. Escribe de 35 a 60 palabras.","prompt_en":"You can't go to your English class tomorrow. Write an email to your teacher, Ms. Lopez. In your email: say that you can't go to class, explain how you feel, say what the doctor told you to do, and ask about the homework. Write 35–60 words.","min_words":35,"max_words":60,"model_answer":"Dear Ms. Lopez,\n\nI'm sorry, but I can't come to class tomorrow. I have a fever and a very bad sore throat. I went to the doctor this afternoon, and she said I should stay in bed for two days. Could you tell me the homework, please? I want to do it at home.\n\nThank you,\nDaniel","checklist_es":["Saludo y despedida adecuados para una maestra","Dices que no irás a clase mañana","Describes tus síntomas con have (I have a fever)","Cuentas el consejo del doctor con should","Preguntas por la tarea con una pregunta amable"]},"speaking":{"read_aloud":["I have a headache and my throat hurts.","You should drink a lot of water and get some rest."],"questions":["What do you usually do when you have a cold?","When was the last time you went to the doctor? What happened?","What should people do to stay healthy? Give some advice."]}},"12":{"reading":{"title":"The trip where everything went wrong","text":"Last month I flew from Guadalajara to Chicago for a work conference, and almost everything that could go wrong did. First, my flight was delayed three hours because of a storm, so I missed my connection in Dallas. The airline staff were very helpful, though. They booked me on the next flight and gave me a voucher for dinner. When I finally landed in Chicago, it was after midnight, and my suitcase wasn't on the baggage carousel. I filled out a form at the lost baggage desk and took a taxi to the hotel.\n\nAt the front desk, the receptionist couldn't find my reservation. I showed her the confirmation email, and she realized the booking was under my company's name, not mine. She apologized and gave me a free upgrade to a suite on the twelfth floor, with a view of the lake.\n\nThe next morning, the airline called to say my bag was on its way. It arrived at the hotel before lunch, so I only had to wear the same shirt for one day. My advice? Always pack a change of clothes and your charger in your carry-on. You never know when you might need them.","questions":[{"q":"Why did the writer miss her connecting flight?","options":["The airline canceled it.","She arrived late at the airport.","Her first flight was delayed.","She lost her passport."],"answer":2,"explain_es":"El primer vuelo se retrasó tres horas por una tormenta, por eso perdió la conexión en Dallas."},{"q":"What did the airline give her in Dallas?","options":["A refund","A seat in first class","A hotel room","A voucher for a meal"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"La aerolínea le dio a voucher for dinner, un vale para cenar."},{"q":"Why couldn't the receptionist find the reservation at first?","options":["It was under the name of her company.","She had never made it.","It was for a different date.","The computer system was down."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"La reservación estaba a nombre de su empresa, no al suyo: under my company's name."},{"q":"What happened to her suitcase?","options":["It was delivered to the hotel the next day.","It stayed in Dallas for a week.","She picked it up at the airport.","It was never found."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"La aerolínea llamó en la mañana y la maleta llegó al hotel antes de la comida."},{"q":"What is the purpose of the writer's advice at the end?","options":["To recommend the hotel in Chicago","To complain about the airline","To tell people to avoid connecting flights","To suggest keeping important things in your hand luggage"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Recomienda llevar ropa extra y el cargador en el equipaje de mano (carry-on) por si pasa algo."}]},"listening":{"title":"Checking in at a hotel","script":[{"who":"A","en":"Good evening, welcome to the Bayview Hotel. Are you checking in?"},{"who":"B","en":"Yes, I have a reservation under Ramírez. Two nights, a double room."},{"who":"A","en":"Let me see... Yes, here it is. Room 418, on the fourth floor. Breakfast is served from six thirty to ten in the restaurant."},{"who":"B","en":"Great. Could you tell me what time checkout is?"},{"who":"A","en":"It's at eleven. If you need a late checkout, it's twenty dollars extra."},{"who":"B","en":"That's fine, I'll let you know. Oh, and would you mind calling a taxi for me tomorrow at seven? I have a meeting downtown."},{"who":"A","en":"No, not at all. The taxi will be waiting at the main entrance."},{"who":"B","en":"Thank you. One more thing, is the Wi-Fi free?"},{"who":"A","en":"Yes, it is. The password is on your key card holder. The elevators are just behind you, on the left."},{"who":"B","en":"Perfect. Thanks so much for your help."}],"questions":[{"q":"How many nights is the guest staying?","options":["Three","One","Two","Four"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"El huésped dice: Two nights, a double room."},{"q":"Which floor is the guest's room on?","options":["The fourteenth","The eighth","The first","The fourth"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"La habitación es la 418, on the fourth floor."},{"q":"What time is checkout?","options":["At six thirty","At eleven","At ten","At seven"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"La recepcionista dice que la salida es a las once. A las diez termina el desayuno."},{"q":"What does the guest ask the receptionist to do?","options":["Change his room","Call a taxi for him","Bring breakfast to his room","Give him a wake-up call"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Pregunta: would you mind calling a taxi for me tomorrow at seven?"},{"q":"Where can the guest find the Wi-Fi password?","options":["In a confirmation email","On the TV in his room","On his key card holder","In the restaurant"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"La recepcionista dice que la contraseña está en el porta tarjeta de la llave."}]},"use":[{"q":"We have three pieces of ___.","options":["luggages","suitcase","baggages","luggage"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Luggage es incontable, por eso se dice three pieces of luggage y nunca luggages."},{"q":"Our flight is ___ because of the fog.","options":["delay","delayed","delaying","late of"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Para retrasos se usa be delayed: our flight is delayed."},{"q":"The plane ___ off at 6:15 this morning.","options":["took","taked","take","taken"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Take off es irregular: el pasado es took off."},{"q":"The reservation is ___ my wife's name.","options":["in","on","under","at"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Para decir a nombre de se usa under: the reservation is under Martínez."},{"q":"I ___ my flight because there was so much traffic.","options":["missed","left","failed","lost"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Perder un vuelo o un camión es miss. Lose es perder un objeto."},{"q":"Would you mind ___ the window, please?","options":["open","opening","to open","opened"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Después de would you mind el verbo va con -ing: would you mind opening...?"},{"q":"___ you help me with my bags, please?","options":["Must","Should","Might","Could"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Could you...? es la forma amable de pedir un favor a un desconocido."},{"q":"Where can I ___ in for my flight to Cancún?","options":["make","get","sign","check"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Registrarse en el aeropuerto o en el hotel es check in."},{"q":"In the US, the ground floor is called the ___ floor.","options":["zero","first","second","base"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"En Estados Unidos la planta baja es el first floor."},{"q":"I'm sorry, ___ the air conditioning in my room isn't working.","options":["but","because","so","and"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Una queja amable suele empezar con I'm sorry, but y luego el problema."}],"writing":{"prompt_es":"Vas a viajar a San Diego. Escribe un correo al hotel para reservar una habitación. Incluye: las fechas y el tipo de habitación, una petición especial, una pregunta sobre el desayuno y una pregunta sobre el transporte desde el aeropuerto. Escribe de 70 a 100 palabras.","prompt_en":"You are planning a trip to San Diego. Write an email to a hotel to book a room. In your email: give the dates and type of room, make a special request, ask about breakfast, and ask about transportation from the airport. Write 70–100 words.","min_words":70,"max_words":100,"model_answer":"Dear Sir or Madam,\n\nI would like to book a double room for three nights, from June 12 to June 15. The reservation should be under the name Ana Torres. Could you give me a quiet room on a high floor, if possible? I'm a light sleeper. I would also like to know if breakfast is included in the price. Finally, my flight lands at 10 p.m., so could you tell me if the hotel has an airport shuttle?\n\nThank you in advance for your help.\n\nBest regards,\nAna Torres","checklist_es":["Saludo y despedida formales (Dear Sir or Madam / Best regards)","Fechas, número de noches y tipo de habitación con book","Una petición especial con could you o would you mind","Pregunta sobre el desayuno","Pregunta sobre el transporte desde el aeropuerto"]},"speaking":{"read_aloud":["My flight was delayed, so I missed my connection in Houston.","Would you mind keeping my luggage at the front desk until this afternoon?"],"questions":["Describe the last time you traveled by plane or by bus. How was it?","What is more important to you in a hotel: location, price or comfort? Why?","Some people say traveling is a waste of money. Do you agree or disagree? Why?"]}},"13":{"reading":{"title":"A message about future plans","text":"Hi Marco,\n\nThanks for your message! I can't believe we're graduating in six weeks. You asked about my plans, so here they are. I'm not going to look for a job right away. Instead, I'm going to spend three months in Canada. I've already found a language school in Toronto, and I'm flying there on August 2nd. My classes start on the 5th, so I'll have a few days to get to know the city first.\n\nAfter Canada, I'm planning to come back to Monterrey and work at my uncle's architecture firm. He says I'll probably start as an assistant, but I don't mind. Hopefully, by this time next year, I'll have saved enough money to buy a car.\n\nWhat about you? Your sister told me you might move to Mexico City. Is that true? If you're free next weekend, would you like to come over for a barbecue? A few people from our class are coming on Saturday at four. I really hope you can make it. I'm looking forward to seeing you!\n\nTake care,\nDaniela","questions":[{"q":"What is Daniela going to do right after she graduates?","options":["Buy a car","Look for a job","Work at her uncle's firm","Study English in Canada"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Dice que no va a buscar trabajo de inmediato; primero se va tres meses a Canadá a una escuela de idiomas."},{"q":"Why is Daniela flying to Toronto on August 2nd?","options":["Because her classes start that day","Because her uncle lives there","To have some time to explore the city before classes","Because the tickets are cheaper"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Sus clases empiezan el 5, así que llega antes para conocer la ciudad unos días."},{"q":"What does she say about the job at the architecture firm?","options":["She will start before she goes to Canada.","She doesn't want to work there.","She will probably start in a junior position.","She is going to be the manager."],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Su tío dice que probablemente empezará como asistente, es decir, en un puesto básico."},{"q":"What does Daniela hope to do by next year?","options":["Move to Mexico City","Live in Canada","Open her own firm","Save enough money for a car"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Usa el futuro perfecto: by this time next year, I'll have saved enough money to buy a car."},{"q":"What do we know about Marco's plans?","options":["He is going to work with Daniela.","He is definitely coming to the barbecue.","He has decided to move to Canada.","He may move to Mexico City."],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Daniela usa might: you might move to Mexico City. Es una posibilidad, no algo seguro."}]},"listening":{"title":"Making weekend plans","script":[{"who":"A","en":"Hey, Luis, what are you doing this Saturday?"},{"who":"B","en":"In the morning I'm helping my dad paint the kitchen. Why?"},{"who":"A","en":"There's a jazz festival in the park. Would you like to come with us in the afternoon?"},{"who":"B","en":"I'd love to, but I think the painting will take all day. Maybe Sunday?"},{"who":"A","en":"The festival is only on Saturday, unfortunately. How about meeting for dinner after you finish, then?"},{"who":"B","en":"That sounds great. I'll probably be done by seven."},{"who":"A","en":"Perfect. I'm going to book a table at that new Korean place on Juárez Street."},{"who":"B","en":"Oh, I've heard it's really good. Should I invite Carla?"},{"who":"A","en":"Sure, but she might be busy. She said she's working late this weekend."},{"who":"B","en":"OK, I'll text her tonight. And don't worry, I won't be late this time, I promise."}],"questions":[{"q":"What is Luis doing on Saturday morning?","options":["Going to the jazz festival","Helping his dad paint the kitchen","Working late","Booking a table"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Luis usa presente continuo para un plan acordado: I'm helping my dad paint the kitchen."},{"q":"Why can't Luis go to the festival?","options":["He thinks he'll be busy all day.","There are no tickets left.","The festival is on Sunday.","He doesn't like jazz."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Dice que la pintura le va a tomar todo el día: the painting will take all day."},{"q":"What time does Luis think he will finish?","options":["By eight","By five","By six","By seven"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Dice: I'll probably be done by seven."},{"q":"What is the woman going to do?","options":["Help paint the kitchen","Invite Carla","Book a table at a Korean restaurant","Buy festival tickets"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Ella dice: I'm going to book a table at that new Korean place."},{"q":"What does Luis promise?","options":["To go to the festival next year","To invite Carla to the festival","To pay for dinner","Not to be late"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Usa will para una promesa: I won't be late this time, I promise."}]},"use":[{"q":"Look at those dark clouds! It ___ rain.","options":["will to","might to","is raining to","is going to"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Cuando hay una evidencia que ves ahora, usa going to: it's going to rain."},{"q":"The phone is ringing. Don't worry, I ___ answer it.","options":["am going to","am answering","will","answered"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Para decisiones tomadas en el momento se usa will: I'll answer it."},{"q":"I'm looking forward to ___ you next week.","options":["saw","be seen","see","seeing"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Después de look forward to va el verbo con -ing, porque to aquí es preposición."},{"q":"Would you like ___ to the movies tonight?","options":["go","going","to go","went"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Después de would you like va to + verbo: would you like to go?"},{"q":"How about ___ pizza tonight?","options":["ordering","order","ordered","to order"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Después de how about el verbo va con -ing: how about ordering?"},{"q":"My train ___ at 7:45 tomorrow morning, so I need to get up early.","options":["leaves","will leaving","leave","is leave"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Para horarios oficiales como trenes o vuelos se usa el presente simple: the train leaves at 7:45."},{"q":"I'm not sure yet, but I ___ go to the beach this weekend.","options":["might to","might","am","will to"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Might expresa posibilidad y va con el verbo base sin to: I might go."},{"q":"This time tomorrow, I ___ on a beach in Cancún.","options":["will lie to","am lie","will have lain","will be lying"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Para una acción en progreso en un momento del futuro se usa will be + -ing."},{"q":"By the end of the year, we ___ the new house.","options":["are finishing by","will finish to","will have finished","finish"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Para algo que ya estará terminado antes de cierto momento se usa will have + participio."},{"q":"Sorry, I can't. I ___ my grandparents on Friday. We arranged it last week.","options":["visit","am visiting","will visiting","visited"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Para planes ya acordados con alguien se usa el presente continuo: I'm visiting my grandparents."}],"writing":{"prompt_es":"Tu amigo estadounidense Jake te escribió: ¿Qué vas a hacer en las vacaciones de verano? Me gustaría visitarte. Contéstale: cuéntale tus planes, invítalo, sugiere algo que pueden hacer juntos y pregúntale cuándo puede venir. Escribe de 70 a 100 palabras.","prompt_en":"Your American friend Jake has written to you: What are you going to do this summer? I'd love to visit you! Write an email to Jake. In your email: tell him about your plans, invite him, suggest something you could do together, and ask when he can come. Write 70–100 words.","min_words":70,"max_words":100,"model_answer":"Hi Jake,\n\nGreat to hear from you! This summer I'm going to work at my aunt's café in the mornings, because I want to save some money. In August, my family is going to spend a week in Oaxaca. Why don't you come and visit us in July? We could go hiking in the mountains, or I could show you the best taco places in my city. I'm sure you'll love it. When is your vacation? Let me know soon so I can tell my parents.\n\nSee you soon,\nAndrés","checklist_es":["Planes decididos con going to","Una invitación clara (Why don't you... / Would you like to...)","Una sugerencia de actividad con could o how about","Una pregunta sobre cuándo puede venir","Saludo y despedida informales"]},"speaking":{"read_aloud":["I'm going to spend the summer working at my uncle's restaurant.","If it doesn't rain, we might have a picnic in the park on Sunday."],"questions":["What are your plans for next weekend?","Where do you think you will be living in five years? Why?","Is it better to plan everything in advance or to be spontaneous? Why?"]}},"14":{"reading":{"title":"From the office to the ocean","text":"Ricardo Fuentes has worked as a diving instructor in Bacalar for six years, but his life used to be very different. 'I used to sit in an office in Mexico City for ten hours a day,' he says. 'I was an accountant, and I was bored all the time.'\n\nIn 2017 he took a vacation in Quintana Roo and tried scuba diving for the first time. 'It was the best day of my life. I had never felt so free,' he remembers. Six months later, he quit his job, sold his car and moved to the coast.\n\nThe first year was hard. He had to get used to earning much less money, and he didn't speak much English, which most of the tourists use. But he has been taking online English classes since he arrived, and his English has improved a lot. 'It's the first time I've really loved my job,' he says.\n\nHas he ever thought about going back? 'Never. My friends from the office have come to visit me, and some of them are jealous!' He has taught more than two thousand students so far, and he has just opened his own diving school.","questions":[{"q":"What was Ricardo's job before he moved?","options":["He sold cars.","He was an accountant.","He was an English teacher.","He was a diving instructor."],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Ricardo dice: I was an accountant, era contador."},{"q":"When did he try scuba diving for the first time?","options":["During a vacation in 2017","Six years ago, in Mexico City","When he was a child","After he quit his job"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"En 2017 se fue de vacaciones a Quintana Roo y buceó por primera vez."},{"q":"What was difficult during his first year?","options":["Finding a place to live","Earning less money and speaking English","Learning how to dive","Missing his family"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Tuvo que acostumbrarse a ganar menos dinero y casi no hablaba inglés."},{"q":"What has Ricardo done recently?","options":["He has sold his car.","He has started English classes.","He has opened his own diving school.","He has gone back to Mexico City."],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Just significa acabar de: he has just opened his own diving school."},{"q":"How do some of his old colleagues feel about his new life?","options":["They wish they had a life like his.","They think he is bored.","They are angry with him.","They are worried about him."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Dice que algunos están jealous, celosos o con envidia, o sea, les gustaría tener su vida."}]},"listening":{"title":"Catching up with an old friend","script":[{"who":"A","en":"Mariana! I haven't seen you in ages. How have you been?"},{"who":"B","en":"Hi, Tom! I've been great, thanks. I've just come back from Japan, actually."},{"who":"A","en":"Japan? Wow! How long were you there?"},{"who":"B","en":"Three weeks. It's the first time I've been to Asia. I went to Tokyo, Kyoto and Osaka."},{"who":"A","en":"Did you eat real ramen? I've always wanted to try it there."},{"who":"B","en":"Oh, yes, almost every day! What about you? Are you still working at the bank?"},{"who":"A","en":"No, I quit last year. I've been working as a web designer since January."},{"who":"B","en":"That's a big change! Do you like it?"},{"who":"A","en":"I love it. I used to hate Mondays, but now I don't mind them at all."},{"who":"B","en":"Good for you! Hey, has your brother gone back to Canada?"},{"who":"A","en":"Yes, he went back in March. He's been living in Vancouver for almost five years now."}],"questions":[{"q":"How long was Mariana in Japan?","options":["Three weeks","Three days","Three months","Five years"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Ella responde: Three weeks."},{"q":"What is true about Mariana's trip?","options":["It was her first time in Asia.","She had been to Asia many times.","She didn't like the food.","She only visited Tokyo."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Dice: It's the first time I've been to Asia."},{"q":"When did Tom start his current job?","options":["In March","Last year","In January","Five years ago"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Tom dice: I've been working as a web designer since January. Renunció al banco el año pasado."},{"q":"How does Tom feel about Mondays now?","options":["He never works on Mondays.","He prefers them to Fridays.","He still hates them.","He doesn't mind them."],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Antes los odiaba (used to hate), pero ahora no le molestan: I don't mind them at all."},{"q":"Where is Tom's brother now?","options":["At Tom's house","At the bank","In Vancouver","In Japan"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Su hermano regresó a Canadá y vive en Vancouver desde hace casi cinco años."}]},"use":[{"q":"Have you ___ been to Oaxaca?","options":["since","yet","ever","already"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Para preguntar por experiencias de vida se usa ever: Have you ever been...?"},{"q":"I haven't finished my homework ___.","options":["already","just","ever","yet"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Yet va al final en negativas y preguntas: I haven't finished yet."},{"q":"We have lived in this apartment ___ 2019.","options":["for","from","during","since"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Since se usa con el momento en que empezó algo (since 2019); for con periodos (for five years)."},{"q":"I ___ that movie last weekend.","options":["saw","have saw","seen","have seen"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Con una fecha terminada como last weekend se usa past simple: I saw."},{"q":"Ana isn't here. She has ___ to the supermarket, but she'll be back soon.","options":["go","gone","went","been"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Has gone to significa que se fue y sigue allá. Has been to significa que fue y ya regresó."},{"q":"I've ___ waiting for the bus for forty minutes!","options":["been","was","be","being"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"El present perfect continuous se forma con have + been + -ing: I've been waiting."},{"q":"It's the first time I ___ sushi.","options":["have eaten","am eating","eat","ate"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Después de It's the first time va present perfect: It's the first time I've eaten..."},{"q":"When I was a kid, I ___ play outside every afternoon.","options":["got used to","use to","was used to","used to"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Used to + verbo base habla de hábitos del pasado que ya no ocurren."},{"q":"It took me months to get used to ___ up at 5 a.m.","options":["get","getting","got","have gotten"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Get used to significa acostumbrarse y va seguido de un verbo con -ing."},{"q":"My English has ___ a lot since I started this course.","options":["improve","improved","improving","improves"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"En present perfect se usa have/has + participio: has improved."}],"writing":{"prompt_es":"Viste este anuncio en una revista en inglés: Buscamos artículos. La mejor experiencia de mi vida. ¿Qué pasó? ¿Por qué fue tan especial? ¿Cómo te cambió? Escribe tu artículo de 70 a 100 palabras.","prompt_en":"You see this announcement in an English-language magazine: Articles wanted! The best experience of my life. What happened? Why was it so special? How has it changed you? Write your article in 70–100 words.","min_words":70,"max_words":100,"model_answer":"A Morning I Will Never Forget\n\nI've traveled to many places, but the best experience of my life happened close to home. Two years ago, my friends and I climbed the Nevado de Toluca at night to see the sunrise. It was freezing, and I almost gave up twice. When the sun finally appeared over the crater lake, everyone went silent. I had never seen anything so beautiful. Since then, I've climbed four more mountains, and I've learned that I'm stronger than I thought. Have you ever tried something that scared you? You should!","checklist_es":["Un título atractivo","Cuentas qué pasó usando past simple con fechas o momentos concretos","Explicas por qué fue especial","Explicas cómo te cambió usando present perfect (Since then, I've...)","Hablas directamente al lector, por ejemplo con una pregunta"]},"speaking":{"read_aloud":["I've never been to Europe, but I've always wanted to go.","We've been living in Puebla since my father changed jobs."],"questions":["What is the most interesting place you have ever visited?","Have you ever done something that really scared you? What happened?","How has your town or city changed in the last ten years?"]}},"15":{"reading":{"title":"Why I love quiet weekends","text":"Most of my friends think I'm boring because I'd rather stay home on Saturday nights than go to a club. To be honest, I used to feel embarrassed about it. Now I don't care. For me, a quiet evening with a good book is far more relaxing than a noisy party, and it's much cheaper too.\n\nDon't get me wrong, I'm not lonely. I just enjoy being alone sometimes. My sister, Paola, disagrees with me. She says going out is the best way to meet people, and she gets bored if she spends more than one night at home. We argue about it all the time, but we both agree on one thing: the worst plan is a night out with people you don't like.\n\nPersonally, I think the important thing is to know yourself. If parties make you nervous, there's no need to force yourself. And if staying home makes you anxious, go out! Last weekend I tried a new board game café near my house. It was quieter than a bar but a lot more fun than my sofa. Was it worth it? Definitely. I'd go again.","questions":[{"q":"How did the writer feel about staying home in the past?","options":["Excited","Scared","Proud","Embarrassed"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"El autor dice: I used to feel embarrassed about it, antes le daba pena."},{"q":"What does the writer say about being alone?","options":["They only do it on weekdays.","It makes them feel sad and lonely.","They enjoy it sometimes, but they aren't lonely.","They hate it, but it's cheaper."],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Dice que no se siente solo ni triste (lonely), solo disfruta estar solo (alone) a veces."},{"q":"What do the writer and Paola agree about?","options":["Going out with people you don't like is the worst plan.","Going out is the best way to meet people.","Board games are boring.","Staying home is more relaxing."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Aunque discuten, coinciden en que lo peor es salir con gente que no te cae bien."},{"q":"What is the writer's main advice?","options":["Spend less money at parties.","Go out every weekend.","Do what suits your personality.","Always stay home on Saturdays."],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Dice que lo importante es conocerte a ti mismo y no forzarte."},{"q":"What did the writer think of the board game café?","options":["It was too expensive.","It was too noisy.","It was worth going and they would go again.","It was more relaxing than staying home."],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Pregunta si valió la pena y responde Definitely. I'd go again."}]},"listening":{"title":"Talking about a new restaurant","script":[{"who":"A","en":"So, what did you think of the new Italian restaurant?"},{"who":"B","en":"Honestly, I was a bit disappointed. The pasta was good, but it was so expensive."},{"who":"A","en":"Really? I thought the prices were OK. It's much cheaper than Bella Roma."},{"who":"B","en":"That's true, but Bella Roma is the best restaurant in the city. The service there is amazing."},{"who":"A","en":"I don't agree. Last time I went to Bella Roma, we waited forty minutes for our food. I was furious."},{"who":"B","en":"Oh no, I didn't know that. That's a shame."},{"who":"A","en":"Anyway, the dessert at the new place was incredible. The tiramisu was worth every peso."},{"who":"B","en":"I agree with you there. It was the most delicious tiramisu I've ever had."},{"who":"A","en":"So, would you go back?"},{"who":"B","en":"Maybe for dessert! But for dinner, I'd rather cook at home."}],"questions":[{"q":"What was the man's main problem with the new restaurant?","options":["It was too expensive.","The service was slow.","It was too far away.","The pasta was bad."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Dice que la pasta estaba buena, pero era muy cara."},{"q":"What does the woman think about the prices?","options":["They are the same as at Bella Roma.","They are too high.","She doesn't remember them.","They are reasonable."],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Ella dice que los precios estaban bien y que es mucho más barato que Bella Roma."},{"q":"Why does the woman disagree about Bella Roma?","options":["It was too expensive.","It was closed.","The food was cold.","She had to wait a long time for her food."],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Esperó cuarenta minutos la comida y se puso furiosa."},{"q":"What do they both agree on?","options":["The dessert was excellent.","The new restaurant is too expensive.","The pasta was the best.","Bella Roma has great service."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Él dice I agree with you there sobre el tiramisú."},{"q":"What will the man probably do?","options":["Go back only for dessert","Go to Bella Roma instead","Go back for dinner","Never go back"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Dice que quizá regrese por el postre, pero para cenar prefiere cocinar en casa."}]},"use":[{"q":"The movie was so ___ that I fell asleep.","options":["bored","boredom","bore","boring"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Los adjetivos con -ing describen lo que causa el sentimiento: the movie was boring."},{"q":"What do you ___ about the new mall?","options":["believe of","think","say of","opinion"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Para pedir opinión se dice What do you think about...?"},{"q":"I ___ with you completely.","options":["agree","agreed to","am agreeing","am agree"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Agree es verbo: I agree. Nunca I am agree."},{"q":"This phone is ___ than my old one.","options":["better","more good","more better","best"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Good tiene comparativo irregular: better. Nunca more better."},{"q":"It's the tallest building ___ the city.","options":["in","of","at","from"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Con superlativos y lugares se usa in: the tallest in the city."},{"q":"My little brother is scared ___ the dark.","options":["about","of","from","with"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Scared lleva la preposición of: scared of the dark."},{"q":"I can't stand ___ in long lines.","options":["waited","to waiting","waiting","wait"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Después de can't stand el verbo va con -ing."},{"q":"I'd rather ___ home tonight.","options":["staying","stay","stayed","to stay"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Would rather va con el verbo base sin to: I'd rather stay."},{"q":"The new apartment is ___ bigger than the old one.","options":["very","too","much","more"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Para reforzar un comparativo se usa much, a lot o a bit. Nunca very bigger."},{"q":"The museum is really worth ___.","options":["visit","visiting","to visit","visited"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Después de worth el verbo va con -ing: it's worth visiting."}],"writing":{"prompt_es":"Tu amiga Emily te escribe: Me aceptaron en dos universidades, una en una ciudad grande y otra en un pueblo pequeño. ¿Cuál crees que debo elegir? Contéstale dando tu opinión, compara las dos opciones y dale un consejo final. Escribe de 70 a 100 palabras.","prompt_en":"Your friend Emily has written to you: I've been accepted at two universities, one in a big city and one in a small town. Which one do you think I should choose? Write an email to Emily. Give your opinion, compare the two options and give her some final advice. Write 70–100 words.","min_words":70,"max_words":100,"model_answer":"Hi Emily,\n\nThanks for asking my opinion! To be honest, I think you should choose the university in the small town. It's much cheaper than the one in the city, and the rent is a lot lower too. In my opinion, it's also easier to make friends in a small place, because everyone knows each other. I know you might get bored at first, but you can always visit the city on weekends. Personally, I'd rather live somewhere quiet and focus on my studies. It's worth it!\n\nGood luck,\nFernanda","checklist_es":["Das tu opinión con I think, In my opinion o Personally","Comparas las opciones con comparativos (cheaper, much easier)","Mencionas una desventaja o el otro punto de vista","Das un consejo final","Saludo y despedida informales"]},"speaking":{"read_aloud":["I was really disappointed with the ending of the movie.","In my opinion, living in a small town is much more relaxing than living in a big city."],"questions":["What makes you feel stressed, and what do you do about it?","What is the best restaurant in your town? Why do you like it?","Do you think social media makes people happier or sadder? Why?"]}},"16":{"reading":{"title":"What recruiters really notice","text":"After fifteen years as a recruiter for a logistics company in Monterrey, Verónica Salas has interviewed more than three thousand candidates. Surprisingly, she says the people who get hired are rarely the ones with the most impressive résumés.\n\n'A résumé gets you through the door, but it doesn't get you the job,' she explains. 'What I'm really listening for is how candidates talk about their mistakes.' According to Salas, many applicants freeze when asked about a project that went wrong, or they simply blame their former boss. The candidates who impress her admit what happened and explain what they would have done differently if they had known more at the time.\n\nShe is equally direct about follow-up emails. In her experience, candidates who send a short thank-you message within twenty-four hours are far more likely to be remembered. However, she warns against sounding desperate. 'One email is professional. Three emails in a week is a red flag.'\n\nSalary negotiation is another area where people make avoidable errors. Rather than naming a figure too early, she recommends asking about the full package first, including benefits and opportunities for training. 'If you accept the first offer without asking a single question, I start to wonder how you'll negotiate with our clients.'\n\nHer final piece of advice may sound obvious, but she insists it is ignored more often than not: research the company before the interview. Nothing ends a conversation faster, she says, than a candidate asking what exactly the company does.","questions":[{"q":"According to Salas, what matters most during an interview?","options":["Asking for a high salary","Having an impressive résumé","How candidates talk about their past mistakes","Getting a reference from a former boss"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Ella dice que lo que realmente escucha es cómo hablan los candidatos de sus errores."},{"q":"Why does the writer use the word 'Surprisingly' in the first paragraph?","options":["Most people would expect the best résumés to get the job.","Salas has interviewed fewer people than expected.","Logistics companies rarely hire new people.","Salas doesn't read résumés at all."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Es una inferencia: lo sorprendente es que no siempre contratan a quien tiene el mejor currículum, que es lo que la mayoría esperaría."},{"q":"What is Salas's view on follow-up emails?","options":["Candidates should send one every day.","Candidates should never send them.","They are only useful for senior positions.","One quick thank-you is good, but too many create a bad impression."],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Recomienda un correo de agradecimiento en 24 horas, pero tres correos en una semana son una señal de alerta (red flag)."},{"q":"Why does Salas worry about candidates who accept the first offer immediately?","options":["It suggests they may not negotiate well for the company.","It shows they don't need the job.","It proves they didn't read the job ad.","It means they will ask for a raise soon."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Se pregunta cómo negociarían con los clientes si no hacen ni una pregunta sobre su propia oferta."},{"q":"What can we infer about a candidate who asks what the company does?","options":["They are very curious and creative.","They want to change departments.","They are likely to get the job.","They haven't prepared properly for the interview."],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Si preguntan eso, demuestran que no investigaron a la empresa, el consejo final del texto."}]},"listening":{"title":"A business phone call","script":[{"who":"A","en":"Good morning, Pacific Logistics. This is Daniel speaking."},{"who":"B","en":"Hi, Daniel, it's Karen Liu from Brightline Foods. Could you put me through to Ms. Ortega, please?"},{"who":"A","en":"I'm afraid she's in a meeting until eleven. Can I take a message?"},{"who":"B","en":"Yes, please. I was wondering if we could move Thursday's meeting to Friday. Our CFO can't make it on Thursday."},{"who":"A","en":"I'll let her know. Friday might be tricky, though. She's flying to Chicago that afternoon, so it would have to be before ten."},{"who":"B","en":"Nine thirty would work for us. If we met at nine thirty, would we have enough time to go through the whole agenda?"},{"who":"A","en":"I think so, as long as the presentation doesn't run over twenty minutes."},{"who":"B","en":"That's fine. Also, would you mind sending me the updated price list beforehand? We'd like to review it with our team."},{"who":"A","en":"Not at all. I'll email it to you this afternoon. And if Ms. Ortega has any problems with Friday, she'll call you back directly."},{"who":"B","en":"Perfect. I really appreciate your help, Daniel."}],"questions":[{"q":"Why can't Karen speak to Ms. Ortega?","options":["She's on vacation.","Karen called the wrong extension.","She's in a meeting.","She's on a plane."],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Daniel dice: I'm afraid she's in a meeting until eleven."},{"q":"Why does Karen want to change the meeting?","options":["She has to fly to Chicago.","The price list isn't ready.","Her CFO isn't available on Thursday.","The agenda is too long."],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Karen explica: Our CFO can't make it on Thursday."},{"q":"Why does the Friday meeting have to be early?","options":["Ms. Ortega is traveling that afternoon.","The office closes at ten.","Karen has another meeting.","The CFO prefers mornings."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Ms. Ortega vuela a Chicago esa tarde, por eso tiene que ser antes de las diez."},{"q":"What does Karen ask Daniel to send her?","options":["The updated price list","The meeting agenda","Ms. Ortega's flight details","The presentation slides"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Pregunta: would you mind sending me the updated price list beforehand?"},{"q":"What will happen if Ms. Ortega can't meet on Friday?","options":["The meeting will stay on Thursday.","She will call Karen herself.","Karen will call again at eleven.","Daniel will cancel the meeting."],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Daniel dice que si hay problema, she'll call you back directly."}]},"use":[{"q":"I have worked ___ marketing for over six years.","options":["at","in","of","on"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Para el área o sector se usa in: I've worked in marketing, experience in sales."},{"q":"I look forward to ___ from you.","options":["hear","hearing","be heard","have heard"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Después de look forward to va -ing: I look forward to hearing from you."},{"q":"If I ___ you, I would ask for a raise.","options":["would be","were","will be","am"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"En el segundo condicional formal se dice If I were you, would + verbo."},{"q":"If we had left earlier, we ___ the train.","options":["would catch","would have caught","had caught","caught"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Tercer condicional: If + had + participio, would have + participio."},{"q":"Could you put me ___ to the sales department, please?","options":["across","up","through","over"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Put someone through significa comunicar o transferir una llamada."},{"q":"Neither side got everything it wanted, but we reached a ___.","options":["compromise","commitment","promise","compromission"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Compromise es un acuerdo donde ambas partes ceden. Commitment es un compromiso u obligación."},{"q":"I'll ___ base with you next week to see how the project is going.","options":["keep","touch","make","get"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Touch base es una expresión de oficina que significa ponerse en contacto brevemente."},{"q":"I would appreciate it ___ you could send the report by Friday.","options":["when","whether","that","if"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"La frase fija es I'd appreciate it if you could..."},{"q":"I will now ___ you the results of the survey.","options":["show","introduce","explain","present"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Show you the results es correcto. Present, explain e introduce necesitan to: present the results to you."},{"q":"Her ___ to work under pressure impressed the interviewers.","options":["unable","enable","able","ability"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Se necesita un sustantivo después de her: ability (habilidad), que viene del adjetivo able."}],"writing":{"prompt_es":"Viste un anuncio para el puesto de Coordinador(a) de Atención al Cliente Bilingüe en una empresa estadounidense. Escribe un correo formal a la gerente de Recursos Humanos, la Sra. Carter. Incluye: tu experiencia, por qué eres buen candidato, cuándo puedes empezar y una pregunta sobre el puesto. Escribe de 120 a 160 palabras.","prompt_en":"You have seen an advertisement for a Bilingual Customer Service Coordinator at an American company. Write an email to the HR manager, Ms. Carter, applying for the job. Include: your relevant experience, why you would be suitable, when you could start, and a question about the position. Write 120–160 words.","min_words":120,"max_words":160,"model_answer":"Dear Ms. Carter,\n\nI am writing to apply for the position of Bilingual Customer Service Coordinator, which I saw advertised on your website.\n\nI have worked in customer service for four years, and I currently lead a team of six agents at a telecommunications company in Guadalajara. In this role, I have handled complaints by phone and email in both English and Spanish, and I have trained new employees. Last year, our team reduced response times by thirty percent.\n\nI believe I would be a good fit for your company because I am organized, patient and comfortable working under pressure.\n\nI am available to start in one month. I was wondering if you could tell me whether the position offers the possibility of working remotely some days.\n\nI look forward to hearing from you.\n\nBest regards,\nMariana Gómez","checklist_es":["Saludo formal (Dear Ms. Carter) y cierre formal (Best regards)","Experiencia con present perfect y past simple bien usados","Razones claras por las que eres adecuado para el puesto","Disponibilidad para empezar","Una pregunta cortés con I was wondering if...","Cierre con I look forward to hearing from you"]},"speaking":{"read_aloud":["I've been working in customer service for five years, and I'm looking for a new challenge.","If we ordered more units, would you be willing to offer us a discount?"],"questions":["Describe your ideal job. What would you be doing every day?","What are the advantages and disadvantages of working for a large company?","Some people say a good salary is the most important thing in a job. How far do you agree?"]}},"17":{"reading":{"title":"Logging off: one week without social media","text":"Last month, after realizing I'd checked my phone over a hundred times in a single day, I decided to try something drastic: one full week without social media, streaming or unnecessary apps. I kept my phone for calls and texts, since my job requires it, but I deleted everything else and asked my team to email me instead.\n\nThe first two days were genuinely uncomfortable. I kept reaching for my phone without thinking, and I felt anxious that I was missing something important. By Wednesday, though, something shifted. I finished a novel I had abandoned months ago, and I noticed I was sleeping better, probably because I was no longer scrolling in bed until midnight.\n\nNot everything was positive. I missed a friend's birthday dinner because the invitation was only posted in a group chat, and I felt terrible when she mentioned it. It made me realize how much of our social lives now depends on platforms that most of us claim to dislike.\n\nWhen the week ended, I didn't go back to my old habits completely. I've reinstalled only two apps, and I've turned off almost all notifications. I also back up my photos manually once a week instead of letting my phone do it automatically, which has made me more aware of how much data I generate.\n\nWould I recommend the experiment? Yes, but with one warning: tell your friends first.","questions":[{"q":"Why did the writer keep her phone during the experiment?","options":["Her friends asked her to keep it.","She wanted to take photos.","She needed it for calls and texts at work.","She needed it to read novels."],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Dice que se quedó con el teléfono para llamadas y mensajes porque su trabajo lo requiere."},{"q":"What changed by the middle of the week?","options":["She stopped going to work.","She felt more anxious than before.","She reinstalled her favorite apps.","She started reading again and slept better."],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Para el miércoles terminó una novela y dormía mejor."},{"q":"Why did the writer miss her friend's birthday dinner?","options":["She forgot the date.","The invitation was shared on an app she wasn't using.","Her friend didn't invite her.","She was working late that night."],"answer":1,"explain_es":"La invitación solo se publicó en un chat grupal, y ella había borrado esas apps."},{"q":"What point does the writer make in the third paragraph?","options":["Group chats should be banned.","Birthday parties are less important than work.","Most people don't use social media anymore.","People depend on social media even though they say they dislike it."],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Se da cuenta de cuánto depende nuestra vida social de plataformas que decimos que no nos gustan."},{"q":"What is the writer's overall attitude to the experiment?","options":["Positive, but she recommends a practical precaution","Completely negative","Neutral, because nothing changed","Enthusiastic, and she has quit all apps forever"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Sí lo recomienda, pero con una advertencia: avisar a tus amigos antes."}]},"listening":{"title":"Tech problems on a video call","script":[{"who":"A","en":"Hi, Sam, can you hear me? Your video keeps freezing."},{"who":"B","en":"Sorry, my connection is really slow today. Is that better? I've turned off my camera."},{"who":"A","en":"Yes, much better. By the way, did you get my email about the new password policy?"},{"who":"B","en":"I did, but I couldn't log in this morning. I think my account got locked."},{"who":"A","en":"That happens if you type the wrong password three times. Did you try resetting it?"},{"who":"B","en":"I tried, but the reset link went to my old email address, the one I don't use anymore."},{"who":"A","en":"OK, I'll ask IT to update it. In the meantime, you can use the shared drive. The server was down earlier, but it's back up now."},{"who":"B","en":"Great. Oh, and should I back up the client files before Friday's update?"},{"who":"A","en":"Definitely. Save everything to the cloud, not just your laptop. Last time, two people lost a whole week of work."},{"who":"B","en":"Got it, Maria. I'll do it this afternoon, as soon as this call is over."}],"questions":[{"q":"Why did Sam turn off his camera?","options":["Maria asked him to save data.","His video kept freezing because of a slow connection.","He was not dressed for work.","His camera was broken."],"answer":1,"explain_es":"La conexión estaba muy lenta y el video se congelaba, así que apagó la cámara."},{"q":"Why couldn't Sam log in this morning?","options":["He forgot his username.","His laptop was broken.","His account was locked.","The server was down."],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Sam dice: I think my account got locked."},{"q":"What was the problem with the reset link?","options":["IT never sent it.","It expired after three minutes.","It was sent to an email address he no longer uses.","It didn't work on his phone."],"answer":2,"explain_es":"El enlace llegó a su correo viejo, el que ya no usa."},{"q":"What does Maria say about the server?","options":["It was down earlier but works now.","It has been hacked.","It will be updated today.","It is still down."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Dice: The server was down earlier, but it's back up now."},{"q":"Why does Maria insist on saving files to the cloud?","options":["Laptops are not allowed at the office.","Some colleagues lost work in a previous update.","The shared drive is full.","The client asked for it."],"answer":1,"explain_es":"La última vez dos personas perdieron una semana completa de trabajo."}]},"use":[{"q":"I can't open the website. I think the server is ___.","options":["broken","off","down","out"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Para decir que un sistema no funciona se usa is down."},{"q":"You're ___ mute, so we can't hear you.","options":["with","at","in","on"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"La frase es you're on mute."},{"q":"I saw the news ___ Instagram this morning.","options":["at","by","in","on"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Con plataformas y redes sociales se usa on: on Instagram, on social media."},{"q":"All the data ___ automatically every night.","options":["is backed up","is backup","are back up","backs up"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Data es incontable (verbo en singular) y aquí se usa pasiva con el phrasal verb back up."},{"q":"My email account ___ last week, so I changed all my passwords.","options":["was hacked","has hacking","hacked","was hack"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Para decir que te robaron la cuenta se usa la pasiva: my account was hacked."},{"q":"You need to ___ before you can download the file.","options":["log in","log on in","logging","login"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Log in separado es el verbo; login junto es el sustantivo."},{"q":"The ___ version of the app has some great new features.","options":["current","actual","present-day of","nowadays"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Actual es falso amigo: significa real. Versión actual se dice current version."},{"q":"I'll ___ you the address when I get home.","options":["text","message to","write","say"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"En EE. UU. text funciona como verbo: I'll text you."},{"q":"I'm trying to cut ___ on screen time before bed.","options":["down","up","off","out"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Cut down on significa reducir algo: cut down on screen time."},{"q":"Teenagers spend far too much time ___.","options":["at online","in online","online","on online"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Online funciona como adverbio y no lleva preposición."}],"writing":{"prompt_es":"En tu clase de inglés hablaron de este tema: La tecnología ha hecho nuestras vidas más estresantes, no más fáciles. Escribe un ensayo dando tu opinión. Habla de: 1. el trabajo, 2. las relaciones personales, 3. una idea propia. Escribe de 120 a 160 palabras.","prompt_en":"In your English class you have been talking about technology. Now your teacher has asked you to write an essay. Technology has made our lives more stressful, not easier. Do you agree? Notes: write about 1. work, 2. relationships, 3. your own idea. Write 120–160 words.","min_words":120,"max_words":160,"model_answer":"It is often said that technology was supposed to make life easier, yet many people feel more stressed than ever. In my view, this is only partly true.\n\nOn the one hand, technology has changed the way we work. Thanks to email and video calls, many people can work remotely, which saves time and money. However, it also means we are always available, and it is hard to disconnect when your boss can text you at ten at night.\n\nOn the other hand, social media has affected our relationships. It allows us to stay in touch with friends who live far away, but it can also make us compare our lives with others and feel anxious.\n\nIn conclusion, I believe technology itself is not the problem. The real issue is how we use it, so we need clear limits, such as turning off notifications after work.","checklist_es":["Introducción que presenta el tema y tu postura","Un párrafo sobre el trabajo con ventajas y desventajas","Un párrafo sobre las relaciones personales","Una idea propia (por ejemplo, poner límites o la privacidad)","Conectores como However, On the other hand, In conclusion","Conclusión clara que responde a la pregunta"]},"speaking":{"read_aloud":["My laptop froze in the middle of the presentation, so I had to restart it.","If you don't back up your files regularly, you might lose everything."],"questions":["Which app could you not live without, and why?","How has technology changed the way people work in your country?","Should children under twelve be allowed to have smartphones? Why or why not?"]}},"18":{"reading":{"title":"From market stall to online store","text":"When Lucía Pérez lost her office job in 2020, she had enough savings to cover three months of rent and very little else. What she did have was her grandmother's recipe for mole and a small kitchen in Puebla. Four years later, her company ships jars of sauce to customers across Mexico and the southern United States.\n\n'At first I sold at a weekend market, and I barely broke even,' she admits. 'After paying for ingredients, the stall and transportation, there was almost no profit.' Instead of giving up, she started tracking every peso in a simple spreadsheet. She discovered that her most popular product was also the one with the lowest margin, so she raised its price slightly. To her surprise, sales hardly dropped.\n\nThe real turning point came when she began selling online. Shipping costs were a constant headache, and an early batch of jars broke in transit, leading to a wave of complaints and refund requests. Rather than arguing with customers, she apologized publicly, replaced every order free of charge and redesigned her packaging. 'It cost me a fortune that month,' she says, 'but many of those customers are still loyal today.'\n\nLucía has turned down two offers from investors who wanted a majority stake in the business. 'They were generous,' she says, 'but I'd rather grow slowly and keep control.' Her advice to future entrepreneurs is refreshingly practical: 'Know your numbers before you worry about your logo.'","questions":[{"q":"What does Lucía mean when she says she 'barely broke even' at first?","options":["She made a large profit.","She broke many jars.","She earned just enough to cover her costs.","She lost all her savings."],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Break even significa no ganar ni perder: apenas cubría sus gastos, casi sin ganancia."},{"q":"What did Lucía's spreadsheet show her?","options":["Online sales were higher than market sales.","Her customers preferred cheaper products.","She was spending too much on rent.","Her best-selling product earned her very little per sale."],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Descubrió que su producto más popular era el que tenía el margen más bajo."},{"q":"How did customers react when she raised the price?","options":["Sales stayed almost the same.","Sales fell dramatically.","Many customers complained.","Sales doubled."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Dice que, para su sorpresa, las ventas casi no bajaron (hardly dropped)."},{"q":"Why does Lucía feel the broken-jar problem was worth the cost in the end?","options":["It made her stop selling online.","The shipping company paid for everything.","It helped her find investors.","Her response won her loyal customers."],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Le costó una fortuna, pero muchos de esos clientes siguen siendo leales hoy."},{"q":"What can we infer about Lucía's attitude toward investors?","options":["She needs money urgently.","She values independence more than fast growth.","She thinks investors are dishonest.","She is waiting for a better offer."],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Rechazó ofertas generosas porque prefiere crecer despacio y mantener el control."}]},"listening":{"title":"A customer service call","script":[{"who":"A","en":"Thank you for calling ShopNow customer service. My name's Andre. How can I help you today?"},{"who":"B","en":"Hi. I ordered a coffee maker two weeks ago, and it still hasn't arrived. The website said delivery would take three to five days."},{"who":"A","en":"I'm sorry to hear that. Could I have your order number, please?"},{"who":"B","en":"Sure, it's 4-7-2-9-1. And I paid nine dollars extra for express shipping."},{"who":"A","en":"Thank you. I can see the package was sent to an old address on your account, on Pine Street."},{"who":"B","en":"Pine Street? I moved out of there in January. I updated my address before I placed the order."},{"who":"A","en":"I apologize. It looks like the system didn't save the change. I can either send you a new coffee maker today or give you a full refund."},{"who":"B","en":"I'd prefer a refund, to be honest. I found one cheaper at a local store anyway."},{"who":"A","en":"Of course. You'll get the full amount, including the shipping fee, back on your credit card within five to seven business days."},{"who":"B","en":"Great. Could you email me a receipt for the refund?"},{"who":"A","en":"Absolutely. You'll receive it in the next few minutes."}],"questions":[{"q":"When did the woman place her order?","options":["Five days ago","In January","Yesterday","Two weeks ago"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Ella dice: I ordered a coffee maker two weeks ago."},{"q":"Why hasn't the package arrived?","options":["It was lost by the shipping company.","The coffee maker was out of stock.","It was sent to her old address.","She gave the wrong order number."],"answer":2,"explain_es":"El paquete se envió a su dirección anterior en Pine Street."},{"q":"What does the woman say about her address?","options":["She had updated it before ordering.","She forgot to change it.","She moved after placing the order.","She still lives on Pine Street."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Dice que actualizó su dirección antes de hacer el pedido, pero el sistema no guardó el cambio."},{"q":"Why does she choose a refund?","options":["She doesn't need a coffee maker anymore.","The agent recommended it.","The new one would take too long.","She found a cheaper one in a local store."],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Prefiere el reembolso porque encontró una más barata en una tienda local."},{"q":"How much money will she get back?","options":["Only the shipping fee","The price of the product plus the shipping fee","Half of the total","Only the price of the product"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Andre dice que recibirá el monto completo, including the shipping fee."}]},"use":[{"q":"I need to ___ some cash from the ATM.","options":["remove","withdraw","take off","retire"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Retirar dinero es withdraw (o take out money). Retire significa jubilarse."},{"q":"I'd love that car, but I can't ___ it right now.","options":["reach","afford","buy for","pay"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"I can't afford it significa no me alcanza. No se dice the money doesn't reach."},{"q":"Can I see your ___? You need it to return the shoes.","options":["recipe","note","receipt","ticket"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"El comprobante de compra es receipt. Ticket es un boleto y recipe una receta de cocina."},{"q":"I'd like to make a ___ about the service I received.","options":["reclamation","complain","claim of","complaint"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Hacer un reclamo es make a complaint. Complain es el verbo."},{"q":"She ___ a lot of money as a software engineer.","options":["earns","wins","wins up","gains to"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Ganar dinero trabajando es earn o make money. Win es para premios o apuestas."},{"q":"The company's ___ grew by 20%, but its profit stayed the same because costs rose.","options":["benefit","budget","revenue","receipt"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Revenue es todo el dinero que entra; profit es lo que queda después de los gastos."},{"q":"We need a 10% down ___ to buy the apartment.","options":["paying","pay","paid","payment"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"El enganche se dice down payment."},{"q":"After two years, my boss finally gave me a ___.","options":["grown","rise up","raise","raising"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Un aumento de sueldo en EE. UU. es a raise."},{"q":"This laptop is very ___ for the quality you get.","options":["afford","affordably","affordability","affordable"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Se necesita un adjetivo: affordable, barato pero bueno. Cheap puede sonar a mala calidad."},{"q":"She left her job to ___ her own business.","options":["start","make up","do","undertake"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Emprender un negocio es start o launch a business; undertake casi no se usa así."}],"writing":{"prompt_es":"Trabajas en una empresa pequeña y tu jefa te pidió un reporte con sugerencias para reducir costos sin afectar la calidad del servicio. Escribe el reporte con títulos para cada sección e incluye una recomendación final. Escribe de 120 a 160 palabras.","prompt_en":"You work for a small company. Your manager has asked you to write a report suggesting ways the company could reduce its costs without affecting the quality of its service. Use headings and include a final recommendation. Write 120–160 words.","min_words":120,"max_words":160,"model_answer":"Introduction\nThe aim of this report is to suggest ways in which our company could reduce its costs without affecting the quality of our service.\n\nOffice expenses\nAt present, we spend a large part of our budget on electricity and office supplies. If employees worked from home two days a week, we could rent a smaller office and save on bills.\n\nSuppliers\nOur contracts with suppliers have not been reviewed for three years. I recommend negotiating new terms or asking for discounts on larger orders. Several competitors have already done this successfully.\n\nTravel\nMany business trips could easily be replaced by video calls, which would save both money and time.\n\nRecommendation\nI would suggest starting with a review of our supplier contracts, as this would have the biggest impact on our profit in the shortest time.","checklist_es":["Introducción que explica el propósito del reporte","Títulos claros para cada sección","Al menos tres sugerencias concretas","Vocabulario de negocios (budget, profit, discount, costs)","Lenguaje formal e impersonal, con condicionales (If..., we could...)","Una recomendación final justificada"]},"speaking":{"read_aloud":["I can't afford a new car right now, so I'm saving for a down payment.","The company's revenue increased last year, but its profits actually fell."],"questions":["Do you prefer shopping online or in stores? Why?","What advice would you give someone who wants to start their own business?","Some people think schools should teach students how to manage money. Do you agree?"]}},"19":{"reading":{"title":"Review: The Salt Road, season one","text":"When it was announced that the bestselling novel The Salt Road would be adapted into a series, fans of the book were nervous. Novels that depend so heavily on a narrator's inner thoughts rarely survive the move to the screen. I'm pleased to report that, for the most part, those worries were unnecessary.\n\nThe eight-episode first season, which was filmed almost entirely on the coast of Baja California, follows Inés, a marine biologist who returns to her hometown after her father disappears at sea. Newcomer Camila Ríos is outstanding in the lead role, and she carries scenes that could easily have felt slow. The supporting cast is solid, although her brother's character is so underwritten that you sometimes forget he's there.\n\nVisually, the show is stunning. The ocean feels both beautiful and threatening, and the soundtrack, composed by a local folk musician, is used sparingly and to great effect. I found myself looking up the lyrics of the opening song after the first episode.\n\nWhere the series stumbles is in its final two episodes. The writers have added a subplot about a corrupt politician that isn't in the book, and it feels rushed and out of place. Readers who loved the novel's ambiguous ending may also be frustrated that everything is explained so neatly here.\n\nStill, these are minor complaints. If you're into slow-burning mysteries, I'd definitely recommend giving it a try. A second season has already been confirmed.","questions":[{"q":"Why were fans of the novel worried about the series?","options":["It was filmed far from the original setting.","The actors were unknown.","The author didn't approve the project.","Books that rely on a narrator's thoughts are hard to adapt."],"answer":3,"explain_es":"El texto dice que las novelas que dependen de los pensamientos del narrador rara vez funcionan en pantalla."},{"q":"What does the reviewer say about the character of the brother?","options":["He only appears in the last episode.","He is the most interesting character.","He is not developed enough.","He was played by a famous actor."],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Underwritten significa que el personaje está poco desarrollado; a veces se te olvida que existe."},{"q":"What does the reviewer suggest about the opening song?","options":["It was too loud and repetitive.","It was taken from a famous movie.","It was only played once.","She liked it so much that she wanted to know the words."],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Buscó la letra (lyrics) después del primer episodio, lo que indica que le gustó mucho."},{"q":"What is the reviewer's main criticism?","options":["The last episodes add a rushed storyline that isn't in the book.","The photography is disappointing.","The acting is weak overall.","The series is too short."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Critica la subtrama del político corrupto en los dos últimos episodios: se siente apresurada y fuera de lugar."},{"q":"Who would the reviewer most likely recommend the series to?","options":["People who enjoy slow mysteries","People who want a fast action series","Children and young teenagers","Only readers of the novel"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Dice: If you're into slow-burning mysteries, I'd definitely recommend giving it a try."}]},"listening":{"title":"Talking about a concert","script":[{"who":"A","en":"Did you end up going to the Natalia Lafourcade concert on Saturday?"},{"who":"B","en":"I did! It was held at the Auditorio Nacional, and honestly, it was one of the best shows I've ever been to."},{"who":"A","en":"Lucky you. The tickets sold out in about ten minutes, so I couldn't get one."},{"who":"B","en":"Seriously? I bought mine the day the tour was announced. Anyway, the audience knew every single song. People were singing the lyrics louder than she was."},{"who":"A","en":"Did she play anything from the new album? I've been listening to it nonstop."},{"who":"B","en":"Only three songs. Most of the set list was older stuff, which I loved. The new album isn't really my thing, to be honest."},{"who":"A","en":"Really? I think it's her most interesting work. The reviews have been great too."},{"who":"B","en":"Maybe I need to give it another chance. Hey, are you watching anything good these days?"},{"who":"A","en":"I just finished a Korean series about a chef. I'd recommend watching it with subtitles, though. The dubbed version is awful."},{"who":"B","en":"Sounds good. Send me the name and I'll check it out this weekend."}],"questions":[{"q":"Why didn't the woman go to the concert?","options":["She doesn't like the singer.","The tickets sold out very quickly.","She had to work on Saturday.","The concert was canceled."],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Ella dice que los boletos se agotaron en unos diez minutos."},{"q":"What impressed the man about the audience?","options":["They were mostly teenagers.","They were very quiet.","They left early.","They sang along very loudly."],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Dice que el público cantaba las letras más fuerte que la cantante."},{"q":"What does the man think of the new album?","options":["The lyrics are too sad.","He hasn't heard it.","It's not really to his taste.","It's her best work."],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Dice: The new album isn't really my thing, o sea, no es de su gusto."},{"q":"How are the two friends' opinions different?","options":["He thinks the reviews are wrong.","She prefers older songs.","He liked the concert more than she did.","She likes the new album much more than he does."],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Ella lo considera su trabajo más interesante; a él no le convence."},{"q":"What does the woman recommend?","options":["Watching a Korean series with subtitles","Watching the dubbed version of a series","Reading the album reviews","Buying concert tickets early"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Recomienda una serie coreana, pero con subtítulos, porque el doblaje es malísimo."}]},"use":[{"q":"Who ___ in the new superhero movie?","options":["acts of","stars","casts","plays of"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Para preguntar quién actúa se dice Who stars in it? o Who's in it?"},{"q":"I fell asleep during ___ five, so I have to watch it again.","options":["chapter","capitule","edition","episode"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"El capítulo de una serie es episode; chapter es solo para libros."},{"q":"The ___ of this song are really beautiful.","options":["letters","words of","letter","lyrics"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"La letra de una canción es lyrics, siempre en plural."},{"q":"The news ___ really surprising today.","options":["were","are","is","have been"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"News es incontable y lleva verbo en singular: the news is."},{"q":"I recommend ___ the book before you see the movie.","options":["to read","reading","you to read","read"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Después de recommend va -ing o that + sujeto: I recommend reading it."},{"q":"The song ___ in a small studio in Oaxaca.","options":["was recorded","was record","has recorded","recorded"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Se grabó se dice con voz pasiva: was recorded (be + participio)."},{"q":"The band's new album ___ next month.","options":["releases","will release","will be released","will be release"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"El álbum no se lanza solo; se usa pasiva en futuro: will be released."},{"q":"We ___ the concert last night and it was amazing.","options":["assisted","attended","assisted to","attended to"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Asistir a un evento es attend. Assist significa ayudar."},{"q":"The ___ applauded for ten minutes after the play ended.","options":["publics","spectating","public","audience"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"El público de un espectáculo es the audience."},{"q":"My grandmother watches a ___ every night at nine.","options":["soap opera","telenovel","novel","romance book"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"La telenovela es a soap opera. Novel es una novela escrita."}],"writing":{"prompt_es":"Un sitio web en inglés busca reseñas de series o películas que recomendarías a otros jóvenes. Escribe una reseña: describe de qué trata, qué te gustó, qué no te gustó tanto y a quién se la recomendarías. Escribe de 120 a 160 palabras.","prompt_en":"You see this announcement on an English-language website: Reviews wanted! Tell us about a series or movie you would recommend to other young people. What is it about? What did you like and not like about it? Who would enjoy it? Write your review in 120–160 words.","min_words":120,"max_words":160,"model_answer":"If you are into stories that make you think, I would strongly recommend the Mexican series Rooftops, which is available on most streaming platforms.\n\nThe series follows three teenage friends who live in the same apartment building in Mexico City in the 1980s. It was filmed on location, and the attention to detail is impressive, from the clothes to the music. The young cast is brilliant, especially the actress who plays Lupita, a shy girl who dreams of becoming a singer.\n\nMy only criticism is that the last two episodes are a bit slow, and one storyline is never fully explained.\n\nOverall, it is a moving and funny show that will appeal to teenagers and their parents alike. Even if dramas aren't usually your cup of tea, give the first episode a try. You might be surprised.","checklist_es":["Introducción que atrae al lector y nombra la serie o película","Resumen breve de la trama sin contar el final","Algo positivo con detalles (actores, música, fotografía)","Una crítica con tacto","Al menos una oración en voz pasiva (It was filmed...)","Recomendación final y a quién le gustaría"]},"speaking":{"read_aloud":["The movie was directed by a young Mexican filmmaker and was released last year.","It's not really my cup of tea, but I can see why so many people love it."],"questions":["What kind of music are you into these days?","Describe a movie or series you would recommend to a friend, and explain why.","Do you think streaming services have been good or bad for the movie industry?"]}},"20":{"reading":{"title":"In defense of changing your mind","text":"There is a peculiar contempt reserved, in public life especially, for people who change their minds. Politicians are accused of flip-flopping; executives who reverse a strategy are seen as weak. Yet the ability to revise one's views in light of new evidence is arguably the defining feature of a mature thinker, not a flaw to be concealed.\n\nPart of the problem, I'd argue, lies in how we frame disagreement. Debates are staged as contests to be won, and conceding a point is treated as losing face. Despite decades of research showing that people rarely abandon a belief when confronted aggressively, we persist in arguing as if volume were a substitute for persuasion. Had we been taught to see a well-made counterargument as a gift rather than an attack, many of our public conversations would look quite different.\n\nNone of this is to suggest that every opinion should be held loosely. Some convictions are rightly firm, and someone who changes position with every passing trend is not so much open-minded as unanchored. The distinction lies in the reason for the change. Shifting because a more compelling piece of evidence has emerged is intellectual honesty; shifting because it has become socially convenient is something else entirely.\n\nWhat, then, would a healthier culture look like? For a start, it would make room for phrases such as 'I hadn't considered that' or 'I may have been wrong' without treating them as admissions of defeat. It would reward leaders who explain why they reconsidered, rather than punishing them for having done so. Eventually, perhaps, we might come to regard the person who has never changed their mind not as admirably consistent, but as someone who has simply stopped paying attention.","questions":[{"q":"What is the writer's main argument?","options":["All opinions should be held loosely.","Revising your views in response to evidence is a sign of maturity.","Public debates are generally productive.","Politicians should never change their minds."],"answer":1,"explain_es":"La idea central es que cambiar de opinión ante nueva evidencia es señal de un pensador maduro, no un defecto."},{"q":"What does the writer suggest about arguing aggressively?","options":["It is necessary in politics.","It has only recently become common.","It is the most effective way to persuade.","It seldom succeeds in changing people's beliefs."],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Menciona investigaciones que muestran que la gente casi nunca abandona una creencia cuando la confrontan de forma agresiva."},{"q":"In the third paragraph, what distinction does the writer make?","options":["Between firm and weak leaders","Between changing views for good reasons and for convenience","Between politicians and executives","Between research and personal experience"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Distingue entre cambiar por evidencia más convincente (honestidad intelectual) y cambiar porque es socialmente conveniente."},{"q":"What does the word 'unanchored' most nearly mean in the text?","options":["Stubborn and inflexible","Extremely open-minded","Well informed","Lacking stable principles"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Por el contexto, alguien que cambia con cada moda no tiene principios firmes que lo sostengan, como un barco sin ancla."},{"q":"What does the final sentence imply about people who never change their minds?","options":["They may no longer be engaging with new information.","They have better arguments than others.","They deserve admiration for their consistency.","They are usually good leaders."],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Es una inferencia irónica: quien nunca cambia de opinión quizá simplemente dejó de prestar atención."}]},"listening":{"title":"After a difficult product launch","script":[{"who":"A","en":"So, be honest with me. What did you make of the launch yesterday?"},{"who":"B","en":"Well, I mean, it wasn't a disaster, but I'm not sure it went quite as well as we'd hoped."},{"who":"A","en":"That's putting it mildly. Half the demo crashed in front of the investors."},{"who":"B","en":"True, but to be fair, nobody could have predicted the server issue. If we'd had another week of testing, we'd probably have caught it."},{"who":"A","en":"Which is exactly what I said back in March. I asked for the deadline to be put off, and I got shot down."},{"who":"B","en":"I remember. And, arguably, you were right. But hindsight is twenty-twenty, you know?"},{"who":"A","en":"I suppose. I just feel like we keep making the same mistake. We promise the moon and then scramble at the last minute."},{"who":"B","en":"Look, let's take this offline and put together a proper review. If we can figure out where the process broke down, we can pitch a more realistic timeline next quarter."},{"who":"A","en":"Fine. But I want leadership kept in the loop this time, not just told after the fact."},{"who":"B","en":"Agreed. I'll set something up for Thursday and make sure they're on the invite."}],"questions":[{"q":"How does the man first describe the launch?","options":["As a great success","As a complete disaster","Diplomatically, admitting it fell short of expectations","As better than the investors expected"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Usa lenguaje suavizado: it wasn't a disaster, but I'm not sure it went quite as well as we'd hoped."},{"q":"According to the man, what could have prevented the problem?","options":["A shorter demo","A different server provider","Fewer investors at the launch","More time for testing"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Usa el tercer condicional: If we'd had another week of testing, we'd probably have caught it."},{"q":"What does the woman imply by mentioning March?","options":["She joined the team in March.","The launch was originally planned for March.","She had already warned that the deadline was unrealistic.","The investors were contacted in March."],"answer":2,"explain_es":"En marzo pidió posponer la fecha límite y rechazaron su propuesta (I got shot down)."},{"q":"What does 'take this offline' mean in this conversation?","options":["Stop using the internet","Cancel the project","Turn off the servers","Discuss it later, separately and in more detail"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Take this offline significa hablar del tema después y en privado, no tiene que ver con internet."},{"q":"What does the woman insist on?","options":["Presenting the review herself","Keeping leadership informed throughout the process","Changing the launch date immediately","Inviting the investors on Thursday"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Quiere que los directivos estén al tanto (kept in the loop) y no que se enteren después."}]},"use":[{"q":"That designer watch must have cost ___.","options":["the head and shoulders","an eye of the face","an arm and a leg","a hand and a foot"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Costar un ojo de la cara en inglés es cost an arm and a leg. Los modismos no se traducen literal."},{"q":"___ the heavy rain, the match went ahead as planned.","options":["Despite of","Despite","However","Although"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Despite va seguido de un sustantivo y nunca lleva of. Although necesitaría un verbo (although it rained)."},{"q":"If I ___ about the traffic, I would have left earlier.","options":["would know","had known","would have known","knew"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Tercer condicional: If + had + participio, would have + participio. Nunca would en la parte del if."},{"q":"We need to ___ a decision by the end of the week.","options":["give","put","do","make"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"La collocation correcta es make a decision, no take ni do."},{"q":"The client isn't ready yet, so we'll have to put ___ until next month.","options":["the meeting off","it out","out the meeting","off it"],"answer":0,"explain_es":"Put off significa posponer. Si el objeto es pronombre va en medio (put it off), nunca put off it."},{"q":"There isn't enough ___ to prove he was involved.","options":["an evidence","evidences","evidence","proofs of"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Evidence es incontable: enough evidence o a piece of evidence, nunca evidences."},{"q":"I'm not sure that's ___ right. Could we check the figures again?","options":["much","so","too","quite"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"I'm not sure that's quite right es una forma suave y educada de decir que algo está mal."},{"q":"After months of negotiations, the two sides ___ reached an agreement.","options":["actually","currently","presently","eventually"],"answer":3,"explain_es":"Eventually significa al final o con el tiempo. Eventualmente en español es occasionally."},{"q":"Our team needs to come ___ a better solution before Friday.","options":["up to","out for","up with","down on"],"answer":2,"explain_es":"Come up with significa idear o proponer una solución. Es un phrasal verb de tres partes."},{"q":"The proposal was rejected due to doubts about its ___.","options":["unfeasible","feasibility","feasibly","feasible"],"answer":1,"explain_es":"Después de its se necesita un sustantivo: feasibility (viabilidad), formado de feasible."}],"writing":{"prompt_es":"Después de un debate en clase, tu profesor te pide un ensayo sobre esta pregunta: ¿Deberían las ciudades prohibir los coches en sus centros históricos? Elige dos de estos aspectos y explica cuál es más importante, con razones: la calidad del aire, los negocios locales, la vida de los residentes. Usa conectores formales y lenguaje matizado. Escribe de 180 a 220 palabras.","prompt_en":"Your class has watched a panel discussion about cities banning cars from their historic centers. You have made the notes below. Notes: air quality, local businesses, residents' quality of life. Write an essay discussing two of the points in your notes. Explain which point you think is more important, giving reasons to support your opinion. Write 180–220 words.","min_words":180,"max_words":220,"model_answer":"In recent years, a number of cities have chosen to close their historic centers to private cars. While the policy is often controversial, I would argue that its benefits clearly outweigh its drawbacks.\n\nThe most compelling argument in its favor concerns air quality. Historic centers tend to have narrow streets in which pollution accumulates, and the evidence linking traffic fumes to respiratory illness is difficult to dispute. Removing cars would not only make these areas healthier but would also help preserve old buildings, which are gradually damaged by exhaust.\n\nOpponents frequently claim that local businesses would suffer if customers could no longer drive to them. This concern is understandable, yet experience elsewhere suggests that it is somewhat exaggerated. Pedestrian streets generally attract more visitors, who tend to stay longer and spend more. Indeed, in several European cities, shop owners who initially protested are now among the plan's strongest supporters.\n\nThat said, such a ban can only succeed if it is accompanied by reliable public transport and adequate access for residents, deliveries and people with disabilities.\n\nOn balance, therefore, I believe air quality is the decisive factor. Provided that the transition is managed carefully, banning cars from historic centers is a measure that cities should seriously consider.","checklist_es":["Introducción con tu postura general","Desarrollas dos de los tres aspectos con argumentos y ejemplos","Presentas y respondes un contraargumento","Conectores formales (however, yet, therefore, that said, despite)","Lenguaje matizado (arguably, somewhat, tend to, I would argue)","Conclusión que dice cuál aspecto es más importante y por qué"]},"speaking":{"read_aloud":["Had I known how tight the deadline was, I would have turned the project down.","Despite the criticism, the proposal arguably remains the most realistic option we have."],"questions":["Tell me about a decision you made that turned out better or worse than you expected.","To what extent should people adapt the way they speak to different situations, such as work, family or social media?","Some argue that experience matters more than formal education. How far would you agree?"]}}};
